my wishes known to you!

248
00:09:39,213 --> 00:09:41,382
You will obey them or die!

249
00:09:42,550 --> 00:09:45,518
Have a pleasant night's
sleep! (laughs evilly)

250
00:09:45,552 --> 00:09:49,123
(Crow laughs)
- How are ya?

251
00:09:50,357 --> 00:09:51,925
- [Crow] Krankor,
nothing to worry about!

252
00:09:51,958 --> 00:09:54,828
Truman Capote sent
to fight Krankor!

253
00:09:54,862 --> 00:09:57,130
(suspenseful music)

254
00:09:57,163 --> 00:09:59,900
- Hey, let's share
your little quarter!

255
00:09:59,933 --> 00:10:02,303
- Hey, Wally!
- What is it, Beave?

256
00:10:02,337 --> 00:10:04,405
- Hot off the press!

257
00:10:04,438 --> 00:10:05,538
- Thanks!

258
00:10:05,572 --> 00:10:06,973
Where are you going?

259
00:10:07,007 --> 00:10:08,808
- Professor Macken's
giving a press conference.

260
00:10:08,842 --> 00:10:11,012
- He's supposed to know
what these space men want.

261
00:10:11,045 --> 00:10:12,780
He might know how we
can fight 'em off, too!

262
00:10:12,813 --> 00:10:14,848
- Yeah, the whole bunch
of firecrackers left over

263
00:10:14,882 --> 00:10:16,383
from last year!

264
00:10:16,417 --> 00:10:18,987
Maybe we can use them!
(laughter)

265
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:20,387
- Let's go, we're late now!
- Goodbye!

266
00:10:20,420 --> 00:10:24,058
- Goodbye!
- Goodbye, unfunny, weird men!

267
00:10:24,092 --> 00:10:25,592
- [Servo] He seems
like a real jerk!

268
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:28,095
- Hey, Wally, I bet you're
afraid of those space men!

269
00:10:28,128 --> 00:10:29,230
- Of course I am!

270
00:10:29,263 --> 00:10:30,163
- What for?

271
00:10:30,197 --> 00:10:31,332
You aren't gonna be much help

272
00:10:31,365 --> 00:10:33,133
if you get frightened
as easy as that!

273
00:10:33,167 --> 00:10:35,335
- [Mike] I'm not here!

274
00:10:35,368 --> 00:10:38,105
- [Servo] Walter
Mondale arrives.

275
00:10:38,138 --> 00:10:39,740
- [Man] Come on, fellas,
shake a leg, we're late!

276
00:10:39,773 --> 00:10:42,810
- [Crow] After swingin' for
some violent porn comics!

277
00:10:42,843 --> 00:10:44,312
- Oh, here he comes now!

278
00:10:44,345 --> 00:10:45,578
- Good morning, Professor!

279
00:10:45,612 --> 00:10:47,415
- [Servo] Mm, it's the
Subway Foundler Club!

280
00:10:47,448 --> 00:10:48,715
- Good morning, gentlemen!
- Welcome to

281
00:10:48,748 --> 00:10:50,450
my Grandma's living room.

282
00:10:50,517 --> 00:10:51,418
- Do you have any questions?

283
00:10:51,452 --> 00:10:52,553
- Yes, Professor.

284
00:10:52,587 --> 00:10:54,022
What about these space men, sir?

285
00:10:54,055 --> 00:10:56,290
Do we expect them to
attempt to land here?

286
00:10:56,323 --> 00:10:58,292
- [Professor] Yes,
let me explain.

287
00:10:58,325 --> 00:10:59,727
You know, gentlemen,

288
00:10:59,760 --> 00:11:01,828
we have developed a
powerful new rocket fuel.

289
00:11:01,862 --> 00:11:04,432
Now, for reasons which
must remain classified,

290
00:11:04,465 --> 00:11:05,867
we believe their visit
has something to do

291
00:11:05,900 --> 00:11:07,033
with this discovery.

292
00:11:07,067 --> 00:11:08,468
- Wait a minute, Professor.

293
00:11:08,502 --> 00:11:10,570
These people are obviously
much more advanced than we are!

294
00:11:10,603 --> 00:11:12,238
What could they
possibly want from us?

295
00:11:12,272 --> 00:11:13,707
- [Reporter] Yes,
they've already achieved

296
00:11:13,740 --> 00:11:17,612
interplanetary space travel,
that's more than we have, sir.

297
00:11:17,645 --> 00:11:19,480
- Ah, it seems
that you are right.

298
00:11:19,513 --> 00:11:21,315
At least about space travel.

299
00:11:21,348 --> 00:11:24,218
In another respect, in
the question of fuel,

300
00:11:24,285 --> 00:11:26,620
their technology
lags far behind ours.

301
00:11:26,653 --> 00:11:28,088
Now, if they were
capable of producing

302
00:11:28,122 --> 00:11:29,790
a rocket fuel like mine,

303
00:11:29,823 --> 00:11:31,725
why, they could
send a hundred ships

304
00:11:31,758 --> 00:11:33,493
to Earth instead of one.

305
00:11:33,527 --> 00:11:37,363
They could conquer the
entire world in a week.

306
00:11:38,432 --> 00:11:41,402
- [Crow] The
Japanese Don Knotts!

307
00:11:41,435 --> 00:11:42,737
- Ah, Jerry, there you are!

308
00:11:42,770 --> 00:11:45,472
- [Servo] Jerry,
baby, ba-bububoom!

309
00:11:45,505 --> 00:11:47,708
- I'm giving you bylines
in the front page!

310
00:11:47,742 --> 00:11:50,010
- [Jerry] Oh, I hope they'll
be someone around to read it!

311
00:11:50,043 --> 00:11:51,578
We've just come
from the war office.

312
00:11:51,612 --> 00:11:53,047
They're declaring
a general alert!

313
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:55,783
- Oh, a general alert!
- Does it affect my bowtie?

314
00:11:55,817 --> 00:11:57,885
- This must be serious!

315
00:11:57,952 --> 00:11:59,753
- They're gonna
try to land here?

316
00:11:59,787 --> 00:12:01,588
- Well, it's not official,

317
00:12:01,622 --> 00:12:03,423
but they're heading
this way, for sure.

318
00:12:03,457 --> 00:12:05,058
- Is that right?

319
00:12:05,092 --> 00:12:06,827
- They're coming here, then.

320
00:12:06,860 --> 00:12:08,028
- [Servo] You're fascinating!

321
00:12:08,062 --> 00:12:10,163
- Gentlemen, this may be
our last day on Earth.

322
00:12:10,197 --> 00:12:13,100
- [Mike] Let's hit
the karaoke bar.

323
00:12:16,303 --> 00:12:18,472
A rare, Godzilla-free day.

324
00:12:20,507 --> 00:12:22,843
- [Police] This is
Metropolitan Police speaking.

325
00:12:22,877 --> 00:12:25,078
Metropolitan Police speaking.
(Servo hums)

326
00:12:25,112 --> 00:12:28,515
All persons are warned
to stay off the streets.

327
00:12:28,548 --> 00:12:32,085
All persons are warned
to stay off the streets.

328
00:12:32,118 --> 00:12:33,320
- [Servo] Paging Mr. Herman.

329
00:12:33,353 --> 00:12:34,455
- [Police] Civil
defense personnel,

330
00:12:34,488 --> 00:12:36,523
report to their stations.

331
00:12:36,557 --> 00:12:39,627
Civil defense personnel,
report to their stations.

332
00:12:39,660 --> 00:12:40,795
- [Servo] Come on!

333
00:12:40,828 --> 00:12:42,195
- [Police] All
others take shelter.

334
00:12:42,228 --> 00:12:44,265
All other persons take shelter.

335
00:12:44,298 --> 00:12:48,302
Do not panic, follow
instructions, you
will not get hurt.

336
00:12:48,335 --> 00:12:50,670
(Crow hums)

337
00:12:52,707 --> 00:12:54,475
- [Man On Radio] Regional
Control reporting.

338
00:12:54,508 --> 00:12:56,910
All Metropolitan sections
are on red alert.

339
00:12:56,943 --> 00:12:59,847
Repeat, all Metropolitan
sections are on red alert.

340
00:12:59,880 --> 00:13:00,982
Over and out.

341
00:13:02,650 --> 00:13:06,720
- [Servo] Stop looking at
us, mind your own business!

342
00:13:06,753 --> 00:13:10,390
- I wonder where Wally is, he
said he would come tonight.

343
00:13:10,423 --> 00:13:13,260
- [Mike] He's got some
stones to mess with me!

344
00:13:13,293 --> 00:13:14,728
- [Crow] Monet in Paris.

345
00:13:14,762 --> 00:13:16,663
(dog barks)

346
00:13:16,697 --> 00:13:19,467
- [Servo] A woferoo, bohow-wow!

347
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:20,733
After that dog!

348
00:13:23,870 --> 00:13:26,973
♪ Wheeeere is arfaro ♪

349
00:13:28,175 --> 00:13:30,643
(Mike laughs)

350
00:13:32,112 --> 00:13:33,747
- One minute to eight.

351
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:35,615
- Is your watch right?

352
00:13:36,483 --> 00:13:38,552
(loud zinging)

353
00:13:38,585 --> 00:13:39,887
- Listen!

354
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:40,922
Here they come!

355
00:13:40,955 --> 00:13:42,088
- [Crow] Is his watch right?

356
00:13:42,122 --> 00:13:44,792
We may never know.
- Come on!

357
00:13:44,825 --> 00:13:48,328
(loud zinging)
- Can you see anything?

358
00:13:48,362 --> 00:13:51,032
- [Servo] (gasps)
The Sony blimp!

359
00:13:51,065 --> 00:13:51,998
(loud zinging)

360
00:13:52,032 --> 00:13:53,500
- [Man] There, look, over there!

361
00:13:53,533 --> 00:13:55,768
- [Servo] It's cheap trick!

362
00:13:58,405 --> 00:14:00,607
- [Mike] Surrender Dorothy!

363
00:14:03,077 --> 00:14:05,980
- [Servo] Same goes
for you, Paris!

364
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:09,783
- [Crow] Pagoda of the Damned!

365
00:14:09,817 --> 00:14:11,552
(loud zinging)

366
00:14:11,585 --> 00:14:14,822
- [Servo] An alien race too
proud to ask for directions.

367
00:14:14,855 --> 00:14:16,790
My baby's sunhat and
smock will protect him!

368
00:14:16,823 --> 00:14:19,493
(Mike chuckles)

369
00:14:21,795 --> 00:14:24,865
- [Crow] Protect
me, Japanese Fabian!

370
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:28,635
(loud zinging)

371
00:14:28,668 --> 00:14:30,170
- Chief!
- What?

372
00:14:30,203 --> 00:14:31,638
- I just got a report
about some strange

373
00:14:31,672 --> 00:14:34,275
electrical disturbance
out in near Beaver Falls.

374
00:14:34,308 --> 00:14:35,108
- You did?

375
00:14:35,142 --> 00:14:37,678
- [Crow] Beaver Falls?

376
00:14:37,712 --> 00:14:40,480
- Oh, let me go,
too, Chief, alright?

377
00:14:40,513 --> 00:14:43,283
- [Servo] Go, you
bizarre little man!

378
00:14:43,350 --> 00:14:47,487
- [Crow] Well, consider
yourself conquered, I gotta go!

379
00:14:48,288 --> 00:14:51,358
("MST3K Love Theme")

380
00:14:54,862 --> 00:14:56,230
- [Man On Radio] Beaver
Falls Control here,

381
00:14:56,263 --> 00:14:58,898
UFO descending in area 220.
- Alright, let's go.

382
00:14:58,932 --> 00:15:01,868
- [Servo] Okay,
uh, yeah, let's go.

383
00:15:02,770 --> 00:15:04,003
(Mike and robots sing)

384
00:15:04,037 --> 00:15:05,572
♪ Oh, here we go off
to Beaver Falls ♪

385
00:15:05,605 --> 00:15:06,473
♪ Beaver Falls ♪

386
00:15:06,507 --> 00:15:07,742
♪ Beaver Falls ♪

387
00:15:07,775 --> 00:15:09,443
♪ Here we go off
to Beaver Falls ♪

388
00:15:09,477 --> 00:15:12,980
♪ So early in the morning ♪

389
00:15:14,213 --> 00:15:16,383
- [Crow] I burned my tofu!

390
00:15:17,517 --> 00:15:18,752
- Something over there!
- Right.

391
00:15:18,785 --> 00:15:20,153
Maintain radio contact
with headquarters.

392
00:15:20,187 --> 00:15:21,588
- Right.

393
00:15:21,622 --> 00:15:24,692
- [Servo] Oh, the Stanley
Cup has invaded Earth!

394
00:15:24,725 --> 00:15:26,360
Aliens, come here right now!

395
00:15:26,393 --> 00:15:27,762
- No, wait.

396
00:15:27,795 --> 00:15:29,297
- It's a periscope.

397
00:15:29,330 --> 00:15:32,165
- Deploy your men around it!
- Right.

398
00:15:32,198 --> 00:15:36,370
- [Crow] I am the lemon
zester of destruction!

399
00:15:37,237 --> 00:15:40,207
(men talk at the same time)

400
00:15:41,408 --> 00:15:43,743
- Hey, there's Macken's car!

401
00:15:44,912 --> 00:15:45,778
- [Servo] That's a
lot more interesting

402
00:15:45,812 --> 00:15:47,113
than a spaceship, a car!

403
00:15:47,147 --> 00:15:48,982
- [Man] Look, look he's
got his kids with him!

404
00:15:49,015 --> 00:15:51,085
- [Man] Hey, Professor
Macken, you're just in time.

405
00:15:51,152 --> 00:15:52,720
The spaceship just
landed over here.

406
00:15:52,753 --> 00:15:54,253
- Yes, I know.

407
00:15:54,287 --> 00:15:55,755
Well, what's going on,
who's in charge here?

408
00:15:55,788 --> 00:15:58,092
- The Commissioner himself but
he's up there investigating.

409
00:15:58,125 --> 00:16:00,127
(men talk at the same time)

410
00:16:00,160 --> 00:16:03,363
- [Servo] Sir,
your office called.

411
00:16:03,397 --> 00:16:04,398
David Byrne!

412
00:16:07,067 --> 00:16:08,202
Hello!

413
00:16:08,235 --> 00:16:09,837
(chuckles) Hello!

414
00:16:09,870 --> 00:16:11,705
- [Mike] Hello, hello?

415
00:16:12,840 --> 00:16:15,875
- [Crow] What message
speaks the drums?

416
00:16:15,908 --> 00:16:18,745
Junior Samples and Business Boy!

417
00:16:18,778 --> 00:16:19,780
- What's the matter
with you, Mickey?

418
00:16:19,813 --> 00:16:21,048
This might be dangerous!

419
00:16:21,082 --> 00:16:23,017
- I'm not afraid, if
you are, go on home!

420
00:16:23,050 --> 00:16:24,952
- [Servo] Wait, those
are two separate ideas!

421
00:16:24,985 --> 00:16:26,620
- [Crow] (chuckles) Yeah!

422
00:16:26,653 --> 00:16:29,490
(rocket whirring)

423
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:34,227
- [Servo] What?

424
00:16:37,530 --> 00:16:38,765
- [Crow] It's a
giant watermelon!

425
00:16:38,798 --> 00:16:40,367
Gallagher's taking over!

426
00:16:40,400 --> 00:16:42,903
(robots gasp)

427
00:16:42,937 --> 00:16:44,738
- [Servo] Okay, good luck,
sir, let me know what hap--

428
00:16:44,772 --> 00:16:46,440
Oh, you want me to go with you.

429
00:16:46,473 --> 00:16:50,110
(loud zing)
(men scream loudly)

430
00:16:50,143 --> 00:16:51,578
- [Servo] I saw some
smoke, it's time for lunch,

431
00:16:51,612 --> 00:16:52,780
look at the street.

432
00:16:52,813 --> 00:16:54,247
- Look, it destroyed
them completely!

433
00:16:54,280 --> 00:16:57,483
- [Crow] Except for
their salad bowls!

434
00:16:57,517 --> 00:17:00,153
- [Phantom] Men of Earth,
this is my first warning!

435
00:17:00,187 --> 00:17:03,423
Do not attempt to come near
or you will be destroyed!

436
00:17:03,457 --> 00:17:06,025
Obey my orders, you are warned!

437
00:17:07,427 --> 00:17:09,697
- [Servo] That is one
crafty parking meter!

438
00:17:09,730 --> 00:17:11,030
- Good Lord!

439
00:17:11,065 --> 00:17:12,232
- Get back to the car.

440
00:17:12,265 --> 00:17:14,300
Notify the Defense Ministry!
- Right!

441
00:17:14,333 --> 00:17:16,537
- [Servo] Remember
to crack a window!

442
00:17:16,570 --> 00:17:18,105
Oh hi, Dave, you here, too?

443
00:17:18,138 --> 00:17:20,707
(loud zings)
(men scream)

444
00:17:20,740 --> 00:17:23,143
- [Crow] I'm not afraid, I'm
wearing a tie, you go home!

445
00:17:23,177 --> 00:17:25,312
- Inspector, Inspector!

446
00:17:25,345 --> 00:17:26,713
Where are you, what happened?

447
00:17:26,747 --> 00:17:27,580
Inspector!

448
00:17:28,682 --> 00:17:31,752
- Look, Commissioner,
this is his gun!

449
00:17:31,785 --> 00:17:32,987
- Follow me!

450
00:17:33,020 --> 00:17:34,988
- [Servo] Wet him
if you got him!

451
00:17:35,022 --> 00:17:36,390
- Take cover, it's dangerous!

452
00:17:36,423 --> 00:17:38,225
Radio car, get the
Defense Ministry quick!

453
00:17:38,258 --> 00:17:39,960
- What happened over there?
- Police force was attacked!

454
00:17:39,993 --> 00:17:42,262
Some kind of a death ray!

455
00:17:42,295 --> 00:17:43,197
- [Man] What's that over there?

456
00:17:43,230 --> 00:17:44,532
Look!

457
00:17:44,565 --> 00:17:47,700
(robots gasp)

458
00:17:47,733 --> 00:17:50,137
- Hey, what's that?
- Looks like a flying saucer!

459
00:17:50,170 --> 00:17:51,338
- [Servo] Meh, looks more like

460
00:17:51,372 --> 00:17:52,840
an upside down
flying wheelbarrow

461
00:17:52,873 --> 00:17:55,475
with a stupa on top but I
guess you could think...

462
00:17:55,508 --> 00:17:58,178
(loud zinging)

463
00:17:58,212 --> 00:18:01,348
- [Crow] Oh, it's
Bucky the spaceship!

464
00:18:05,085 --> 00:18:06,187
(loud explosion)

465
00:18:06,220 --> 00:18:08,755
- [Servo] Holy
Santa, pray for us!

466
00:18:11,658 --> 00:18:13,160
Ha, made you duck!

467
00:18:16,230 --> 00:18:20,167
What is that thing, you
go home hats are good?

468
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:21,368
- [Crow] Hello!

469
00:18:21,402 --> 00:18:22,368
(suspenseful music)

470
00:18:22,402 --> 00:18:25,105
- [Servo] Grown ups of the corn!

471
00:18:25,138 --> 00:18:28,242
Mitch Gaylord.
(Mike laughs)

472
00:18:28,275 --> 00:18:29,977
- What's that, a man?
- Mm-hm.

473
00:18:30,010 --> 00:18:32,078
- [Crow] Believe it or not, yup.

474
00:18:32,112 --> 00:18:34,515
(triumphant music)

475
00:18:34,548 --> 00:18:36,783
- [Servo] The king approacheth!

476
00:18:36,850 --> 00:18:39,720
- Phantom of Krankor,
hear my words!

477
00:18:39,753 --> 00:18:42,055
I warn you to leave this planet.

478
00:18:42,088 --> 00:18:43,423
You are not wanted here.

479
00:18:43,457 --> 00:18:45,892
I warn you for the last time!

480
00:18:45,925 --> 00:18:48,395
- [Servo] And by the
last, I mean first.

481
00:18:48,428 --> 00:18:51,465
(wind blows loudly)

482
00:18:51,498 --> 00:18:53,167
(loud zinging)

483
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:57,370
- [Crow] I have no powers but
I can skip reasonably well!

484
00:18:58,938 --> 00:19:00,340
- Oh?

485
00:19:00,373 --> 00:19:01,875
- [Masked Man] Your weapons are
useless against me, Phantom!

486
00:19:01,908 --> 00:19:04,978
You are merely exhausting
your energy supply!

487
00:19:05,012 --> 00:19:07,180
You must leave
the Earth at once!

488
00:19:07,213 --> 00:19:09,850
- [Servo] Alright,
let me talk to him.

489
00:19:09,917 --> 00:19:12,018
- Get him on the
televiser, quick!

490
00:19:12,052 --> 00:19:13,820
- [Servo] But I'm
spinning my salad.

491
00:19:13,853 --> 00:19:15,155
- It is enough that I know you.

492
00:19:15,188 --> 00:19:16,490
You are Phantom of Krankor

493
00:19:16,523 --> 00:19:18,058
and you wish to
rule the universe!

494
00:19:18,092 --> 00:19:19,693
- [Crow] He's gonna get
grass stains on his Danskins!

495
00:19:19,727 --> 00:19:21,895
- You are planning now to
destroy the whole world!

496
00:19:21,928 --> 00:19:23,597
I won't let you go
through with this!

497
00:19:23,630 --> 00:19:25,265
You will not get
what you've come for!

498
00:19:25,298 --> 00:19:27,700
You might as well leave now!

499
00:19:27,733 --> 00:19:28,835
- But who are you?

500
00:19:28,868 --> 00:19:29,670
Tell me!

501
00:19:29,703 --> 00:19:30,503
Who are you?

502
00:19:30,537 --> 00:19:31,705
What's your name?

503
00:19:31,738 --> 00:19:33,273
- [Masked Man] I
am Prince of Space!

504
00:19:33,307 --> 00:19:36,510
(robots gasp giddily)
- Wait a moment!

505
00:19:36,543 --> 00:19:37,443
- [Servo] Larry, we got anything

506
00:19:37,477 --> 00:19:40,047
on this Price of Space guy?

507
00:19:40,080 --> 00:19:42,015
(loud ding)

508
00:19:42,048 --> 00:19:44,417
- [Crow] Powered by rotted
fish, I will defeat you!

509
00:19:44,483 --> 00:19:47,320
(loud zinging)

510
00:19:47,353 --> 00:19:49,122
- [Servo] My contacts
is bothering me!

511
00:19:49,155 --> 00:19:52,392
(high pitched whistling)

512
00:19:52,425 --> 00:19:54,160
- Captain, look at
the atom machine!

513
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:55,562
- The plutonium

514
00:19:55,595 --> 00:19:57,130
