and we believe it is
still in this area now.

593
00:23:04,183 --> 00:23:05,085
- Hi!

594
00:23:05,118 --> 00:23:06,820
- Hello, late this morning, huh?

595
00:23:06,853 --> 00:23:08,822
- Last night, what
happened to you?

596
00:23:08,855 --> 00:23:10,090
- Last night?

597
00:23:10,123 --> 00:23:11,725
Oh, an old friend asked
me to go out to dinner.

598
00:23:11,758 --> 00:23:13,260
- Hey, Wally, you missed it.

599
00:23:13,293 --> 00:23:15,228
I saw Prince of
Space last night.

600
00:23:15,262 --> 00:23:16,930
He chased away the spacemen!
- I like that kid.

601
00:23:16,963 --> 00:23:18,665
He's good.
- Here's the whole story,

602
00:23:18,698 --> 00:23:19,867
right here!

603
00:23:19,900 --> 00:23:21,968
You can read it in
this morning's paper.

604
00:23:22,002 --> 00:23:24,303
- Listen, Wally, do you
think that Prince of Space

605
00:23:24,337 --> 00:23:25,805
really comes from a star?

606
00:23:25,838 --> 00:23:26,773
- I guess so.

607
00:23:26,807 --> 00:23:28,007
- Thank you!

608
00:23:28,040 --> 00:23:28,875
- Why not?

609
00:23:28,908 --> 00:23:30,410
What do you think?

610
00:23:30,443 --> 00:23:32,745
The Prince of Space might
just be a man like Wally?

611
00:23:32,778 --> 00:23:34,247
- [Crow] Woody
Allen asked me out.

612
00:23:34,280 --> 00:23:36,683
- [Wally] In a way he is,
if you think about it.

613
00:23:36,717 --> 00:23:38,752
After all, I believe
in peace, too.

614
00:23:38,785 --> 00:23:40,920
I'd be willing to fight
this Phantom character,

615
00:23:40,953 --> 00:23:42,155
same way as he did.

616
00:23:42,188 --> 00:23:43,657
- [Mickey] Ha-ha, you
wouldn't fight him!

617
00:23:43,690 --> 00:23:44,858
You're too scared!

618
00:23:44,892 --> 00:23:46,693
- [Servo] Are we gonna
work at all today?

619
00:23:46,727 --> 00:23:47,927
- [Wally] Going where?

620
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:50,463
- [Mickey] Over to
Johnnie's house.

621
00:23:50,497 --> 00:23:51,732
- [Mike] Let's get outta here.

622
00:23:51,765 --> 00:23:54,367
- [Crow] Let's go
to Johnnie's house.

623
00:23:54,400 --> 00:23:56,068
I like it very much!

624
00:23:58,838 --> 00:24:01,340
(doors close)

625
00:24:09,615 --> 00:24:11,518
- Oh yeah, Mike, I was
wondering that myself.

626
00:24:11,552 --> 00:24:12,785
Weird, isn't it?

627
00:24:12,818 --> 00:24:13,820
- Oh hey, Tom--

628
00:24:13,853 --> 00:24:14,787
How'd you get here so fast?

629
00:24:14,822 --> 00:24:16,022
- Oh, he'll be along. (laughs)

630
00:24:16,055 --> 00:24:17,290
I have his chicken puppet!

631
00:24:17,323 --> 00:24:18,992
- Hey, where's Crow?
- Talking like what?

632
00:24:19,025 --> 00:24:20,260
- Why are you talking like that?

633
00:24:20,293 --> 00:24:22,195
- No, I'm not, I'm just
way ahead of you, Mike!

634
00:24:22,228 --> 00:24:23,897
- Well, like that, you're
answering my questions

635
00:24:23,930 --> 00:24:25,365
before I ask 'em.

636
00:24:25,398 --> 00:24:26,800
I don't know, I'm just
asking him the same thing.

637
00:24:26,833 --> 00:24:28,235
- No, you dope!

638
00:24:28,268 --> 00:24:30,070
I mean I'm moving faster
than you temporally speaking!

639
00:24:30,103 --> 00:24:31,905
- Hey, what do you mean
you're way ahead of me?

640
00:24:31,938 --> 00:24:33,940
- Well, I asked you for it,
Crow, you were right here!

641
00:24:33,973 --> 00:24:35,142
- Hi, guys!

642
00:24:35,175 --> 00:24:37,043
Hey, how'd you get here so fast?

643
00:24:37,077 --> 00:24:38,312
- That's what I've been
trying to tell you, Mike!

644
00:24:38,345 --> 00:24:40,313
I'm ahead of you by
about three seconds!

645
00:24:40,347 --> 00:24:41,582
- You know what, guys?

646
00:24:41,615 --> 00:24:42,515
I think there may
be something wrong

647
00:24:42,548 --> 00:24:44,017
with the space-time continuum?

648
00:24:44,017 --> 00:24:45,685
- Servo, how'd you
get my chicken puppet?

649
00:24:45,718 --> 00:24:47,053
- Woof, sorry!

650
00:24:47,087 --> 00:24:48,522
Everything's on the fritz!

651
00:24:48,555 --> 00:24:50,423
My burrito was done before
I put it in the oven!

652
00:24:50,457 --> 00:24:52,392
- Alright, alright, take
your damn chicken puppet!

653
00:24:52,425 --> 00:24:54,827
I'll have it back before
you know it anyway! (laughs)

654
00:24:54,862 --> 00:24:56,362
- Okay, Tom, why don't you just
give him his chicken puppet

655
00:24:56,395 --> 00:24:57,630
back, alright?
- Say, why don't

656
00:24:57,663 --> 00:24:59,565
we ask Gypsy to mess
with the warp engine?

657
00:24:59,598 --> 00:25:02,902
- Well's all I know is I
want my chicken puppet back!

658
00:25:02,935 --> 00:25:04,170
Hey, how'd that happen?

659
00:25:04,203 --> 00:25:05,672
- That's a good idea.

660
00:25:05,705 --> 00:25:07,673
Gypsy, there's something wrong
with the space-time thingie.

661
00:25:07,707 --> 00:25:09,175
Isn't there anything we can do?

662
00:25:09,208 --> 00:25:11,678
- Well, okay, Gypsy, I guess
all we can do is ride it out.

663
00:25:11,712 --> 00:25:13,213
I'm outta here.

664
00:25:13,247 --> 00:25:14,613
- Okay, Gypsy, I guess all
we can do is ride it out.

665
00:25:14,647 --> 00:25:15,582
I'm g--

666
00:25:15,615 --> 00:25:17,083
Wow, that's a weird déjà vu.

667
00:25:17,117 --> 00:25:19,152
(Tom laughs)

668
00:25:19,185 --> 00:25:20,887
Yeah, that's a good
idea, Crow, you do that.

669
00:25:20,920 --> 00:25:21,722
This is really weird.

670
00:25:21,755 --> 00:25:23,155
We'll be right back.

671
00:25:23,188 --> 00:25:24,257
- Well, I'm just gonna
play with my chicken puppet

672
00:25:24,290 --> 00:25:25,758
till this blows over.

673
00:25:25,792 --> 00:25:26,827
I'll see you, Mike!

674
00:25:26,860 --> 00:25:29,762
Tom! (whistles)

675
00:25:29,795 --> 00:25:32,398
(loud zinging)

676
00:25:36,035 --> 00:25:39,605
Hey, anybody seen
my chicken puppet?

677
00:25:39,638 --> 00:25:42,708
("MST3K Love Theme")

678
00:25:46,545 --> 00:25:49,015
- [Servo] Sugar,
nature's rich bounty,

679
00:25:49,048 --> 00:25:50,750
helping the war effort!

680
00:25:50,750 --> 00:25:52,485
- [Mike] Still lagging
behind, Crow, huh?

681
00:25:52,518 --> 00:25:54,320
- [Crow] Shut up.

682
00:25:54,353 --> 00:25:57,423
You know, a "scare me" would
really help things out here.

683
00:25:57,457 --> 00:25:59,792
(chuckles) "Scare me".

684
00:25:59,825 --> 00:26:03,997
- [Servo] It's a Sealy
Posture-Pedic cornfield!

685
00:26:05,165 --> 00:26:06,065
- [Crow] All those
Heaven's Gate people

686
00:26:06,098 --> 00:26:06,900
were supposed to meet us here.

687
00:26:06,933 --> 00:26:10,203
(suspenseful music)

688
00:26:10,237 --> 00:26:11,470
- [Servo] We have to
chop the (mumbles)

689
00:26:11,503 --> 00:26:14,207
and then get to the invasion!

690
00:26:14,240 --> 00:26:17,110
- [Mike] Today's lotto
numbers are seven.

691
00:26:17,143 --> 00:26:18,612
- Careful now.

692
00:26:18,645 --> 00:26:20,947
This microwave search will
help us locate that Prince.

693
00:26:20,980 --> 00:26:21,948
- Mm-hm.

694
00:26:21,982 --> 00:26:23,383
- We'll find him.

695
00:26:24,583 --> 00:26:26,753
That miserable scum.
- He stole my cup!

696
00:26:26,787 --> 00:26:29,088
(Mike laughs)

697
00:26:29,122 --> 00:26:31,057
- When I find him, I'm
gonna kill him myself!

698
00:26:31,090 --> 00:26:33,660
- [Servo] Uh, I was actually
signed up to do that, sir.

699
00:26:33,693 --> 00:26:35,128
- Oh, here he is!

700
00:26:36,963 --> 00:26:38,398
- [Henchman] Location
four and a half miles

701
00:26:38,432 --> 00:26:39,798
northwest of here.

702
00:26:39,832 --> 00:26:44,003
(mumbles) 37.2, inside
a concrete building.

703
00:26:45,172 --> 00:26:47,007
Strong iron reaction.
- Can I move this thing,

704
00:26:47,040 --> 00:26:48,408
thanks.

705
00:26:48,442 --> 00:26:51,143
- Hmm, that puts him
near Macken's laboratory!

706
00:26:51,177 --> 00:26:52,345
Hey!

707
00:26:52,378 --> 00:26:54,647
See if you can get
him on the telefinder!

708
00:26:54,680 --> 00:26:57,683
(Servo hums Pop Goes the Weasel)

709
00:26:57,750 --> 00:27:00,887
- [Servo] Luxury
retirement compounds!

710
00:27:02,788 --> 00:27:04,457
- Right over there, sir!

711
00:27:04,490 --> 00:27:05,325
- Mm-hm.

712
00:27:06,727 --> 00:27:08,795
- [Crow] Well, I'm back from
break, anything shaking?

713
00:27:08,828 --> 00:27:10,763
- Let's go get 'em!

714
00:27:10,797 --> 00:27:12,398
Break out the underground tank!

715
00:27:12,432 --> 00:27:15,802
- [Servo] Round the
underpants for a change!

716
00:27:15,835 --> 00:27:17,770
- [Henchman]
Attention, below there!

717
00:27:17,803 --> 00:27:19,872
Prepare the underground tank!

718
00:27:19,905 --> 00:27:22,408
Coordinate 602--
- Oh, oh, oh.

719
00:27:25,045 --> 00:27:26,212
- [Mike] What gets into

720
00:27:26,245 --> 00:27:28,147
some civilizations?
- I don't know.

721
00:27:28,180 --> 00:27:29,815
- Pretty small cubicles!

722
00:27:29,848 --> 00:27:32,785
- [Johnnie] I've been watching
all morning, but it's no use!

723
00:27:32,818 --> 00:27:34,220
- [Mickey] Why not?

724
00:27:34,253 --> 00:27:34,987
- [Johnnie] I think he
only comes around at night!

725
00:27:35,022 --> 00:27:36,522
- [Mickey] Why?

726
00:27:36,555 --> 00:27:38,625
- He's evil and evil people
always come around at night!

727
00:27:38,658 --> 00:27:41,127
- Nobody's watching, they
even come in the daytime.

728
00:27:41,160 --> 00:27:42,328
- [Crow] Although, when
evil people are mating,

729
00:27:42,362 --> 00:27:44,463
