737
00:28:06,018 --> 00:28:08,655
What are we, a bunch of women?

738
00:28:08,688 --> 00:28:10,557
- Hey, that looks
like that space man.

739
00:28:10,590 --> 00:28:11,792
Remember the other night?

740
00:28:11,825 --> 00:28:12,625
- You're right!

741
00:28:12,658 --> 00:28:13,827
We'll go see, come on!

742
00:28:13,860 --> 00:28:15,562
- [Servo] I have a trial
at three, let's go!

743
00:28:15,595 --> 00:28:17,797
- Take these, will you?
- Wait!

744
00:28:17,830 --> 00:28:19,032
Where are you going now?

745
00:28:19,065 --> 00:28:20,367
- We're gonna spy
on those space men!

746
00:28:20,400 --> 00:28:23,268
They're in the old factory!
- What?!

747
00:28:23,302 --> 00:28:26,305
(suspenseful music)

748
00:28:27,473 --> 00:28:28,942
- [Crow] We filled
out pants, sir!

749
00:28:28,975 --> 00:28:30,377
(Tom and Mike laugh)

750
00:28:30,410 --> 00:28:34,113
- [Servo] Ready and mince,
mince, mince, mince,

751
00:28:34,147 --> 00:28:37,750
mince, mince, mince,
mince, mince, mince....

752
00:28:41,053 --> 00:28:42,155
- [Crow] Wait, this
isn't where we parked--

753
00:28:42,188 --> 00:28:44,857
Oh yeah, upper level, come on.

754
00:28:44,890 --> 00:28:47,893
- [Servo] The Caped
Caplain Brigade!

755
00:28:49,628 --> 00:28:51,765
Aha, and now the real
reason we came here!

756
00:28:51,798 --> 00:28:53,332
Refurbishing old
buildings and selling them

757
00:28:53,365 --> 00:28:55,635
as affordable condominiums!

758
00:29:00,540 --> 00:29:03,208
(Prince laughs)

759
00:29:04,277 --> 00:29:06,012
- [Crow] Raceway park!

760
00:29:06,045 --> 00:29:07,147
- You came.

761
00:29:07,180 --> 00:29:09,315
I've been expecting you!

762
00:29:09,348 --> 00:29:11,283
- I came, yes.

763
00:29:11,283 --> 00:29:14,320
(Prince laughs)
And now I'm going to kill you!

764
00:29:14,353 --> 00:29:15,255
- Ha-ha! Oh--
- Just how

765
00:29:15,288 --> 00:29:17,090
do you propose to do that?

766
00:29:17,123 --> 00:29:21,027
Your ray guns will have no
effect on me or my ship!

767
00:29:21,060 --> 00:29:22,462
I've told you that already.
- Hold on,

768
00:29:22,495 --> 00:29:24,797
I'm gettin' a
Dodger's game here.

769
00:29:24,830 --> 00:29:26,665
- You'd better leave
this planet in peace.

770
00:29:26,698 --> 00:29:28,502
I warned you once before.

771
00:29:28,535 --> 00:29:30,002
- Kill him!

772
00:29:30,035 --> 00:29:32,905
(loud zing)
(loud explosion)

773
00:29:32,938 --> 00:29:35,908
- [Crow] Come on, little buddy!

774
00:29:35,942 --> 00:29:37,577
- Where did he go?
- He disappeared!

775
00:29:37,610 --> 00:29:39,012
- No, in here, he must be here!

776
00:29:39,045 --> 00:29:41,413
(Tom pants heavily)
- He's gone.

777
00:29:41,447 --> 00:29:43,550
- The coward, he ran away.

778
00:29:43,583 --> 00:29:45,452
- Looking for me?
- Uh, yeah we are,

779
00:29:45,485 --> 00:29:47,353
hi!
- I'm not running away.

780
00:29:47,387 --> 00:29:49,588
No, I wanna stay because
I'm gonna prevent you

781
00:29:49,622 --> 00:29:51,457
from getting Dr.
Macken's formula!

782
00:29:51,490 --> 00:29:53,358
- Kill him!
- Would you guys just listen?

783
00:29:53,392 --> 00:29:56,095
Your guns don't work! (sighs)
- Some of you

784
00:29:56,128 --> 00:29:57,830
go that way!
- Aagh!

785
00:29:57,863 --> 00:29:59,432
- Aaagh!

786
00:29:59,465 --> 00:30:01,000
- Bring the laser cannon!

787
00:30:01,033 --> 00:30:03,035
- The Prince is there!
- Yeah, he must be fighting

788
00:30:03,068 --> 00:30:04,570
with that Phantom!

789
00:30:06,805 --> 00:30:08,842
- [Crow] Somebody left a
perfectly good refrigerator

790
00:30:08,875 --> 00:30:12,578
over there! (laughs)

791
00:30:12,612 --> 00:30:14,180
- [Henchman] Here's
the laser cannon, sir.

792
00:30:14,213 --> 00:30:15,382
- Good.

793
00:30:15,415 --> 00:30:16,850
- [Henchman] We
can't find him, sir!

794
00:30:16,917 --> 00:30:17,917
- Listen!

795
00:30:17,950 --> 00:30:19,385
Show yourself!

796
00:30:19,418 --> 00:30:21,553
Otherwise we're gonna
kill some different!

797
00:30:21,587 --> 00:30:23,055
- Some different?
- Different?

798
00:30:23,088 --> 00:30:23,923
- [Prince] I hear you!

799
00:30:23,957 --> 00:30:25,123
Come in here!

800
00:30:25,157 --> 00:30:26,993
I'm waiting for you!

801
00:30:27,027 --> 00:30:28,562
Leave the children alone!

802
00:30:28,595 --> 00:30:30,630
- [Crow] You hear
that, Jerry Seinfeld?

803
00:30:30,663 --> 00:30:33,700
- [Prince] You cannot harm them
anyway as long as I am here!

804
00:30:33,733 --> 00:30:36,002
- [Mike] Do you need a ladder?

805
00:30:36,035 --> 00:30:38,170
- I've got you now, you scum!

806
00:30:38,203 --> 00:30:39,605
(Mike and robots laugh)
- Scum?

807
00:30:39,638 --> 00:30:42,175
- [Servo] Where'd
that come from?

808
00:30:42,208 --> 00:30:44,910
- This is the end for you!
- Ya jerk!

809
00:30:44,943 --> 00:30:49,115
- You'll be a horrible example
for anyone who opposes me!

810
00:30:50,082 --> 00:30:51,283
- [Servo] Really
horrible example

811
00:30:51,317 --> 00:30:52,618
because no one else will
ever be scared of him.

812
00:30:52,652 --> 00:30:55,187
(loud zinging)

813
00:30:56,288 --> 00:30:58,625
- (laughs) I told you.

814
00:30:58,658 --> 00:31:00,660
Your weapons have
no effect on me!

815
00:31:00,693 --> 00:31:02,195
- [Servo] It is my
considerate advice

816
00:31:02,228 --> 00:31:04,663
that you discontinue your
use of said weapon! Ha-ha!

817
00:31:04,697 --> 00:31:08,067
(Phantom shouts)
- See, you are scum!

818
00:31:08,100 --> 00:31:09,735
(Mike laughs)

819
00:31:09,768 --> 00:31:13,138
- [Mike] I'll throw
my doll at you!

820
00:31:13,172 --> 00:31:14,840
- Let's go!

821
00:31:14,873 --> 00:31:17,643
(dramatic music)

822
00:31:18,745 --> 00:31:20,980
- [Servo] Tiniwee-yuway!

823
00:31:21,013 --> 00:31:23,515
- Hey wait, you go that way!

824
00:31:23,548 --> 00:31:26,452
(children shout)
(Mike and robots laugh)

825
00:31:26,485 --> 00:31:28,253
- [Crow] You know, this is where
your cram school experience

826
00:31:28,287 --> 00:31:30,122
really comes in handy!

827
00:31:31,757 --> 00:31:35,362
We have to get back
to bootblacking, we
like it very much!

828
00:31:35,395 --> 00:31:37,963
- Please, don't let
him take me, please!

829
00:31:37,997 --> 00:31:39,498
- [Servo] Empirical data
suggests the accuracy

830
00:31:39,532 --> 00:31:41,000
of my earlier contention

831
00:31:41,033 --> 00:31:44,503
that your weapons against
me are without merit!

832
00:31:46,005 --> 00:31:48,473
- [Crow] Ooh, ouchie, ouchie,
ouchie, ouchie, ooh, ow, ooh!

833
00:31:48,507 --> 00:31:50,208
- You're a good shot!

834
00:31:50,242 --> 00:31:53,378
(dramatic music)

835
00:31:53,412 --> 00:31:55,113
- [Servo] Oof, my lumbar!

836
00:31:55,147 --> 00:31:56,382
- Oh!
(Crow laughs)

837
00:31:56,382 --> 00:31:58,685
- Come here!
- Help, help, Prince, help me!

838
00:31:58,718 --> 00:32:01,853
- [Crow] Again,
detention is thwarted.

839
00:32:01,887 --> 00:32:05,292
- [Servo] Please,
call me the artist!

840
00:32:05,325 --> 00:32:06,125
- Did you get hurt?

841
00:32:06,158 --> 00:32:07,127
Are you both alright?

842
00:32:07,160 --> 00:32:08,795
- Yes, Prince!
- Yes, Prince!

843
00:32:08,828 --> 00:32:11,397
Oh boy, you beat up that
Phantom pretty good!

844
00:32:11,430 --> 00:32:12,498
- Yes.

845
00:32:12,532 --> 00:32:14,033
Don't wanna kill him though.

846
00:32:14,067 --> 00:32:16,168
Listen, the police are
coming, we'd better go now.

847
00:32:16,202 --> 00:32:17,737
- Right.

848
00:32:17,770 --> 00:32:19,838
(sirens wail faintly)

849
00:32:19,872 --> 00:32:21,907
- [Servo] It's so chilly
I brought my shawl.

850
00:32:21,940 --> 00:32:23,643
- Johnnie, listen to me.

851
00:32:23,677 --> 00:32:24,977
I wanna give you something.

852
00:32:25,010 --> 00:32:26,678
Keep it with you always.

853
00:32:26,712 --> 00:32:29,982
If you ever need me again,
just turn the dial, understand?

854
00:32:30,048 --> 00:32:31,317
- I'll turn the dial!

855
00:32:31,350 --> 00:32:32,518
- [Servo] If you need me!

856
00:32:32,552 --> 00:32:34,387
- You won't tell
anybody about this.

857
00:32:34,420 --> 00:32:35,488
Agreed?
- Yes.

858
00:32:35,522 --> 00:32:37,157
- Alright, goodbye now.

859
00:32:37,190 --> 00:32:40,025
- [Crow] (chuckles) Who we
gonna tell first? (chuckles)

860
00:32:40,058 --> 00:32:41,293
- Hey, there's the Commissioner!

861
00:32:41,327 --> 00:32:42,395
- [Servo] Pete Rosseau?

862
00:32:42,428 --> 00:32:44,463
(footsteps echo loudly)

863
00:32:44,497 --> 00:32:47,300
- [Mike] (chuckles)
Wow, tap dogs!

864
00:32:47,333 --> 00:32:49,402
- Look, there's the
kid! Hey, Mickey!

865
00:32:49,435 --> 00:32:50,670
- Commissioner!
- Commissioner!

866
00:32:50,703 --> 00:32:52,305
- Commissioner!
- Well, what's going on?

867
00:32:52,338 --> 00:32:54,507
- The Prince of Space and
Phantom, they were fighting!

868
00:32:54,540 --> 00:32:56,308
- Phantom got beat
up and ran away!

869
00:32:56,342 --> 00:32:57,543
- What'd you say?

870
00:32:57,577 --> 00:32:58,812
The Prince of Space?
(Crow laughs)

871
00:32:58,845 --> 00:32:59,978
- The one who has
the flying saucer.

872
00:33:00,012 --> 00:33:01,213
- Yeah!
- The one you saw last night?

873
00:33:01,247 --> 00:33:02,548
- Yeah, that's right!
- And he was here today?

874
00:33:02,582 --> 00:33:03,750
- Yeah! Right, Johnnie?

875
00:33:03,817 --> 00:33:06,885
- Mm-hm!
- Good job not telling, kids!

876
00:33:06,918 --> 00:33:08,822
- He even spoke with us,
you know what he said?

877
00:33:08,855 --> 00:33:11,390
- Yeah, he said the space
men came here to Earth

878
00:33:11,423 --> 00:33:13,793
(mumbles) the Mackens'
new rocket fuel.

879
00:33:13,827 --> 00:33:15,995
- [Servo] Yeah, the big
goomba's gonna take the fuel!

880
00:33:16,028 --> 00:33:17,797
- [Policeman] Look at this!

881
00:33:17,830 --> 00:33:19,965
- [Crow] Terry got my gun dirty!

882
00:33:19,998 --> 00:33:22,035
- One of those space
men was using that!

883
00:33:22,068 --> 00:33:23,568
- One of those space men?
- Chief!

884
00:33:23,602 --> 00:33:25,472
- The building is empty!

885
00:33:25,505 --> 00:33:27,107
- They all got away, huh?

886
00:33:27,140 --> 00:33:28,140
Come on, your father's
worried about you.

887
00:33:28,173 --> 00:33:29,242
- Alright.
- Take over.

888
00:33:29,275 --> 00:33:31,443
- [Servo] Yeah, right, whatever.

889
00:33:31,477 --> 00:33:35,648
- [Crow] Wow, it's a really
modern Lutheran Church!

890
00:33:36,815 --> 00:33:37,583
- [Servo] They're
gonna pop in here

891
00:33:37,617 --> 00:33:38,718
for some sushi burritos.

892
00:33:39,552 --> 00:33:41,120
- [Johnnie] Dr. Sangamon!

893
00:33:41,153 --> 00:33:43,155
- [Doctor] What is it, boys?

894
00:33:43,188 --> 00:33:44,390
- Please, sir.

895
00:33:44,423 --> 00:33:45,858
Are you going to go
ahead with the tests?

896
00:33:45,892 --> 00:33:46,792
- Of course we are.

897
00:33:46,825 --> 00:33:47,893
- Everything's ready, doctor.

898
00:33:47,927 --> 00:33:49,028
- Good.
- You can run

899
00:33:49,062 --> 00:33:50,463
a swab out the
particle accelerator?

900
00:33:50,497 --> 00:33:51,763
- Oh listen, boys.

901
00:33:51,797 --> 00:33:52,965
I

902
00:33:52,998 --> 00:33:55,133
think you'd be
better off at home.

903
00:33:55,167 --> 00:33:56,368
There's no danger, of course,

904
00:33:56,402 --> 00:33:59,538
but we don't want
any chances, right?

905
00:33:59,572 --> 00:34:00,840
- If this Phantom shows up,

906
00:34:00,873 --> 00:34:02,542
these soldiers aren't
gonna be much good.

907
00:34:02,575 --> 00:34:03,743
- Yeah.

908
00:34:03,777 --> 00:34:05,177
I wish Prince of Space
was here with us.

909
00:34:05,210 --> 00:34:06,545
- Did you bring
the die with you?

910
00:34:06,578 --> 00:34:07,447
- Why, sure.

911
00:34:07,480 --> 00:34:08,680
- Why don't we call him with it?

912
00:34:08,713 --> 00:34:10,115
Then we're not in
any trouble, really,

913
00:34:10,148 --> 00:34:12,085
but we don't wanna
take any chances.

914
00:34:12,118 --> 00:34:14,853
- [Crow] What the hell
happened to my pants?

915
00:34:14,887 --> 00:34:16,555
- I'm gonna tell him
it was your idea.

916
00:34:16,588 --> 00:34:17,823
- Mm-hm.

917
00:34:17,857 --> 00:34:20,827
- [Servo] So if we get
busted, it's your ass!

918
00:34:20,860 --> 00:34:23,328
(kids shout)

919
00:34:23,362 --> 00:34:25,432
You're a handsome woman.

920
00:34:25,465 --> 00:34:27,367
- Lawrence, what was that noise?

921
00:34:27,400 --> 00:34:28,367
- [Lawrence] Did
you hear a noise?

922
00:34:28,400 --> 00:34:29,602
- Mm-hm.

923
00:34:29,635 --> 00:34:31,170
- [Lawrence] I only
hear the turbines.

924
00:34:31,203 --> 00:34:32,037
- I see.

925
00:34:33,405 --> 00:34:35,007
- Look, it's him, the Phantom!

926
00:34:35,040 --> 00:34:37,243
- Ha-ha, the little
troublemakers, huh?

927
00:34:37,277 --> 00:34:38,377
- [Mike] When chickens attack!

928
00:34:38,410 --> 00:34:40,412
(kids shout in pain)

929
00:34:40,447 --> 00:34:43,482
("MST3K Love Theme")

930
00:34:47,887 --> 00:34:49,088
- Goodbye.
- I'm retiring

931
00:34:49,122 --> 00:34:50,355
and moving to Florida!

932
00:34:50,388 --> 00:34:52,825
- Well, this is a
great day for us!

933
00:34:52,858 --> 00:34:54,493
- [Servo] Jimmy Osmond!

934
00:34:54,527 --> 00:34:56,462
(dramatic music)

935
00:34:56,495 --> 00:34:59,565
(loud zinging)
- The day is less great now!

936
00:34:59,598 --> 00:35:02,568
- No! (screams)

937
00:35:02,602 --> 00:35:04,537
- [Servo] For some reason,
that doesn't work on hats!

938
00:35:04,570 --> 00:35:05,705
- [Professor] Who are you,

939
00:35:05,738 --> 00:35:06,505
what do you want?
- You know what I want!

940
00:35:06,538 --> 00:35:08,240
Your rocket fuel.

941
00:35:08,273 --> 00:35:09,775
Those soldiers who
are standing there

942
00:35:09,808 --> 00:35:12,845
are good examples of what my
ray guns can do, Professor.

943
00:35:12,878 --> 00:35:14,480
So don't try my patience!
- But do try

944
00:35:14,513 --> 00:35:16,182
my homemade griddle cakes.

945
00:35:16,215 --> 00:35:18,217
- Well, are you going to
talk or do you want me

946
00:35:18,250 --> 00:35:20,252
to start with the children?

947
00:35:20,285 --> 00:35:22,155
- There's a safe right here!

948
00:35:22,188 --> 00:35:23,857
- Get moving!

949
00:35:23,890 --> 00:35:24,790
- [Crow] I thought you
said you were gonna start

950
00:35:24,823 --> 00:35:27,193
with the (chuckles) children!

951
00:35:27,227 --> 00:35:28,962
- Mars, puts guards on the door.

952
00:35:28,995 --> 00:35:31,163
- Yes, sir.
- Mars?

953
00:35:31,197 --> 00:35:34,267
(kids shout)

954
00:35:34,300 --> 00:35:35,568
- [Crow] Didn't they
consider taking over

955
00:35:35,602 --> 00:35:37,670
one of the Earth's good nations?

956
00:35:37,703 --> 00:35:39,972
- Well, what are
you waiting for?

957
00:35:40,005 --> 00:35:41,507
I want that safe opened!

958
00:35:41,540 --> 00:35:42,875
- [Mike] Oh, sorry,
I'm a little out of it.

959
00:35:42,908 --> 00:35:46,212
I stayed up and watched
Letterman last night.

960
00:35:46,245 --> 00:35:48,513
(triumphant music)
Please, mister!

961
00:35:48,547 --> 00:35:50,415
Cram school at three a.m.!

962
00:35:50,415 --> 00:35:53,385
(dramatic music)

963
00:35:53,418 --> 00:35:57,557
- [Crow] If I can only
reach this dried squid!

964
00:35:58,723 --> 00:36:00,760
- [Servo] Oh, the
secret armoire!

965
00:36:01,993 --> 00:36:04,430
- [Crow] Whoops, my doorknob!

966
00:36:05,565 --> 00:36:06,998
- [Phantom] Ha,
this is what I want!

967
00:36:07,032 --> 00:36:09,035
- [Servo] The abstracted
deed and your late crappity!

968
00:36:09,068 --> 00:36:12,905
(kids shout indistinctly)

969
00:36:12,938 --> 00:36:14,973
Give me that remote!

970
00:36:15,007 --> 00:36:16,675
- Help us, Prince!
- Prince!

971
00:36:16,708 --> 00:36:18,310
- [Servo] Allow me to
reference my earlier codicil

972
00:36:18,343 --> 00:36:20,312
on how your weapons
are ineffective!

973
00:36:20,345 --> 00:36:21,180
- Enough!

974
00:36:22,147 --> 00:36:23,182
There's no use firing.

975
00:36:23,215 --> 00:36:24,717
Your guns won't work against me!

976
00:36:24,750 --> 00:36:25,952
- [Crow] Have I mentioned that?

977
00:36:25,985 --> 00:36:29,122
- And Phantom, give the
bag back to the Doctor.

978
00:36:29,155 --> 00:36:30,522
- [Servo] Argh, what
a bunch of crap.

979
00:36:30,557 --> 00:36:31,357
- Take him!

980
00:36:31,390 --> 00:36:32,892
(henchmen shout)

981
00:36:32,925 --> 00:36:34,527
- Prince!
- Prince!

982
00:36:34,560 --> 00:36:36,362
- [Crow] They all
have me goiters.

983
00:36:36,395 --> 00:36:38,898
(henchmen shout)

984
00:36:38,932 --> 00:36:41,267
- Prince, you saved us!
- Stand clear, boys.

985
00:36:41,300 --> 00:36:43,102
- Move on, Johnnie,
you're going with me!

986
00:36:43,135 --> 00:36:44,803
- Prince, help!
- One move, he'll die!

987
00:36:44,837 --> 00:36:46,772
- No! Let the boy go!

988
00:36:46,805 --> 00:36:47,740
Take the formula!

989
00:36:47,773 --> 00:36:49,042
Let the boy go!

990
00:36:49,075 --> 00:36:50,475
- [Servo] So, am I your hostage?

991
00:36:50,508 --> 00:36:51,310
Should I--

992
00:36:51,343 --> 00:36:53,012
Oh,
(loud explosion)

993
00:36:53,045 --> 00:36:55,782
(soldiers shout)

994
00:36:56,648 --> 00:36:57,717
Aha! I guess.

995
00:37:00,953 --> 00:37:04,557
- [Crow] Medical Center,
starring Evel Knievel!

996
00:37:04,590 --> 00:37:07,092
(sirens wail)

997
00:37:08,293 --> 00:37:09,162
- [Servo] They were
supposed to meet me

998
00:37:09,195 --> 00:37:10,797
here in the saucer!

999
00:37:12,732 --> 00:37:14,467
- [Crow] Air Krankor!

1000
00:37:17,637 --> 00:37:19,038
(loud zing)
(loud explosion)

1001
00:37:19,072 --> 00:37:20,538
- [Servo] Oh, Krankor blew
up a potential tackler

1002
00:37:20,572 --> 00:37:24,743
in the 40 and now there's
nothing but daylight!

1003
00:37:26,145 --> 00:37:29,048
Their invasion is like
poorly planned bank heist!

1004
00:37:30,482 --> 00:37:31,583
- [Crow] (chuckles) You
just opened up a whole can

1005
00:37:31,617 --> 00:37:34,587
of jellied whoop ass, pal!

1006
00:37:34,620 --> 00:37:36,055
- [Mike] You know,
I'll never go by

1007
00:37:36,088 --> 00:37:38,623
a switching station without
thinking of this scene.

1008
00:37:38,657 --> 00:37:40,525
(loud zing)
(loud explosion)

1009
00:37:40,558 --> 00:37:41,793
- [Crow] Your guns are useless

1010
00:37:41,827 --> 00:37:44,163
but scare the crap
out of me anyway!

1011
00:37:44,197 --> 00:37:47,333
- [Servo] There's trouble
at the church of the bomb!

1012
00:37:47,367 --> 00:37:49,035
(loud zing)
(loud explosion)

1013
00:37:49,068 --> 00:37:50,535
- Oh!

1014
00:37:50,568 --> 00:37:53,272
- [Crow] So, you gonna let me
invade your planet now, huh?

1015
00:37:53,305 --> 00:37:54,140
Huh?

1016
00:37:56,075 --> 00:37:57,643
- No, not that, don't touch--

1017
00:37:57,677 --> 00:37:59,145
- [Servo] You can't use the
phone, it doesn't dial out!

1018
00:37:59,178 --> 00:38:00,612
- Don't touch it!

1019
00:38:01,513 --> 00:38:03,048
Help!

1020
00:38:03,048 --> 00:38:07,118
- [Mike] The easily
bamboozled Prince of Space.

1021
00:38:07,152 --> 00:38:10,923
- [Servo] Meanwhile in
a carwash in Yokahama.

1022
00:38:10,957 --> 00:38:12,825
(suspenseful music)

1023
00:38:12,858 --> 00:38:14,993
(loud blast)
- Alright, that's fine,

1024
00:38:15,027 --> 00:38:17,295
it's fine, we got
fire insurance!

1025
00:38:17,330 --> 00:38:18,763
It's alright!

1026
00:38:18,797 --> 00:38:20,432
- [Servo] Never even
had time to tell Houston

1027
00:38:20,465 --> 00:38:22,335
that they had a problem.

1028
00:38:22,368 --> 00:38:24,170
Oh, the inanity!

1029
00:38:24,203 --> 00:38:26,838
- [Crow] Oh, the
Japan-ity! (chuckles)

1030
00:38:26,872 --> 00:38:30,642
(siren wails)
- Aww, that's a shame!

1031
00:38:30,677 --> 00:38:32,678
- Dr. Macken! Dr. Macken!

1032
00:38:32,712 --> 00:38:33,912
How horrible!

1033
00:38:33,945 --> 00:38:35,413
He blew up the ship!

1034
00:38:35,447 --> 00:38:38,017
Look, there they go now!

1035
00:38:38,050 --> 00:38:39,918
- [Servo] People looking
very Spielberg-ian!

1036
00:38:39,952 --> 00:38:41,520
- Oh! The Prince of Space!

1037
00:38:41,553 --> 00:38:43,155
He's going after them!

1038
00:38:43,188 --> 00:38:45,223
(loud zinging)

1039
00:38:45,257 --> 00:38:46,258
- [Crow] Yes, I
am Prince of Space

1040
00:38:46,292 --> 00:38:48,460
and I am going after them!

1041
00:38:49,762 --> 00:38:52,130
- [Servo] And his
companion, Duke of Puddles!

1042
00:38:52,163 --> 00:38:54,767
(loud zinging)

1043
00:38:56,368 --> 00:38:58,037
He sent us some cinnamon rolls!

1044
00:38:58,070 --> 00:39:01,240
There's the icing and the dough
is usually under the icing.

1045
00:39:01,273 --> 00:39:02,107
Here.

1046
00:39:02,975 --> 00:39:04,843
Okay, let's see here!

1047
00:39:04,877 --> 00:39:06,212
Dear Japan, bite me.

1048
00:39:06,245 --> 00:39:07,647
Love, Prince of Space!
- I will bring back

1049
00:39:07,680 --> 00:39:10,750
the formula after I chase
these invaders home.

1050
00:39:10,783 --> 00:39:13,352
Signed, Prince of Space.

1051
00:39:13,385 --> 00:39:14,353
- [Crow] In the
meantime, there may be

1052
00:39:14,387 --> 00:39:16,555
many more horrible deaths.

1053
00:39:17,823 --> 00:39:18,657
Um, Torva?

1054
00:39:20,192 --> 00:39:21,393
- [Pilot] Your
attention, please.

1055
00:39:21,427 --> 00:39:23,128
You're in our flight
from San Francisco

1056
00:39:23,162 --> 00:39:25,563
will land at International
Airport in 15 minutes.

1057
00:39:25,597 --> 00:39:28,000
Please observe the no
smoking sign when it is lit.

1058
00:39:28,033 --> 00:39:29,502
Thank you.

1059
00:39:29,535 --> 00:39:31,237
- [Servo] Man, what an ugly
bunch of kids, they yours?

1060
00:39:31,270 --> 00:39:33,205
- Doctor, I think you
dropped this photograph.

1061
00:39:33,238 --> 00:39:34,573
- Oh, thank you!

1062
00:39:35,440 --> 00:39:36,808
- That's your sister, isn't it?

1063
00:39:36,842 --> 00:39:38,710
She'd never forgive
you if you lost it.

1064
00:39:38,743 --> 00:39:42,347
- [Servo] Yeah, uh, don't
talk to me anymore, alright?

1065
00:39:42,380 --> 00:39:45,918
(loud zinging)
- A giant roast turkey!

1066
00:39:45,952 --> 00:39:48,387
- [Servo] Do you
want the window seat?

1067
00:39:48,420 --> 00:39:51,423
(suspenseful music)

1068
00:39:52,925 --> 00:39:54,693
Hey, that lady
got extra peanuts!

1069
00:39:54,727 --> 00:39:58,063
- [Crow] And she got
the whole can, too!

1070
00:40:00,365 --> 00:40:03,602
(hums a cheerful tune)

1071
00:40:05,737 --> 00:40:07,172
- You want me, sir?

1072
00:40:07,205 --> 00:40:08,740
- [Chief] Ah, Captain
Munakata, come in, please.

1073
00:40:08,773 --> 00:40:10,375
- [Servo] I understand
you're stuffed with cheese.

1074
00:40:10,408 --> 00:40:12,545
- I want you to investigate
the disappearance

1075
00:40:12,578 --> 00:40:15,580
of a civilian aircraft,
you understand?

1076
00:40:15,613 --> 00:40:16,482
- Yes, sir.

1077
00:40:16,515 --> 00:40:17,950
- [Man] About 10 minutes ago,

1078
00:40:17,983 --> 00:40:20,452
our radio contact with
the plane was interrupted.

1079
00:40:20,485 --> 00:40:22,455
- [Crow] Who's
talking? (chuckles)

1080
00:40:22,488 --> 00:40:23,555
- [Man] At the time,
it must have been

1081
00:40:23,588 --> 00:40:25,723
approaching--
- Are we hearing voices?

1082
00:40:25,757 --> 00:40:27,660
- Point Barrow?
- We believe so.

1083
00:40:27,693 --> 00:40:29,262
- [Munakata] I'll
go, immediately.

1084
00:40:29,295 --> 00:40:31,430
- [Servo] Or Thursday.

1085
00:40:31,463 --> 00:40:32,998
- Munakata.

1086
00:40:33,032 --> 00:40:34,167
Be careful.

1087
00:40:34,200 --> 00:40:36,468
- Yes, sir, I will.
- Love you!

1088
00:40:36,502 --> 00:40:37,970
(loud zoom)

1089
00:40:38,003 --> 00:40:39,938
- [Munakata] Baker tower
from dog charlie 22,

1090
00:40:39,972 --> 00:40:41,373
come in.
- Woof, over.

1091
00:40:41,407 --> 00:40:43,108
- [Man In Radio] Baker
tower here, go ahead.

1092
00:40:43,142 --> 00:40:46,145
- [Munakata] Altitude 10,000
feet, Point Barrow dead ahead.

1093
00:40:46,178 --> 00:40:47,412
Nothing in view.

1094
00:40:47,445 --> 00:40:50,248
Will circle and
investigate, over.

1095
00:40:50,282 --> 00:40:51,983
- [Man In Radio]
Roger, over and out.

1096
00:40:52,017 --> 00:40:54,787
- [Crow] I'm a wasp, over. Bzzt!

1097
00:40:54,820 --> 00:40:57,155
(loud zoom)

1098
00:41:00,827 --> 00:41:02,828
- [Servo] Hey,
it's Stevie Wonder!

1099
00:41:02,862 --> 00:41:06,232
♪ Isn't she lovely ♪

1100
00:41:06,265 --> 00:41:09,435
♪ Isn't she wonderful ♪

1101
00:41:12,170 --> 00:41:14,440
(shouts in pain)
(Mike and robots laugh)

1102
00:41:14,473 --> 00:41:15,573
- [Munakata] Baker tower!

1103
00:41:15,607 --> 00:41:17,075
Baker tower!

1104
00:41:17,108 --> 00:41:18,310
I can't move!

1105
00:41:18,343 --> 00:41:19,178
I--

1106
00:41:21,013 --> 00:41:22,582
I can't move!

1107
00:41:22,615 --> 00:41:23,915
- [Servo] Wait,
sorry, I can move!

1108
00:41:23,948 --> 00:41:25,817
I just forgot how for a second!

1109
00:41:25,852 --> 00:41:26,852
- Dog charlie!

1110
00:41:26,885 --> 00:41:27,720
Dog charlie!

1111
00:41:27,753 --> 00:41:29,388
What's the matter?

1112
00:41:29,422 --> 00:41:31,323
Hello, dog charlie!

1113
00:41:31,357 --> 00:41:32,558
Come in, please!

1114
00:41:32,592 --> 00:41:34,960
What's the matter?
Can you read me?

1115
00:41:34,993 --> 00:41:36,362
- [Munakata] I can't move!

1116
00:41:36,395 --> 00:41:37,663
My instruments!

1117
00:41:39,365 --> 00:41:40,598
My instruments

1118
00:41:40,632 --> 00:41:41,867
are going haywire!

1119
00:41:41,900 --> 00:41:44,168
- [Mike] My violin,
my tuba, haywire!

1120
00:41:44,203 --> 00:41:45,637
- What's the matter?

1121
00:41:45,670 --> 00:41:47,773
- [Munakata]
Controls are locked!

1122
00:41:47,807 --> 00:41:49,608
- Munakata, what's the matter?

1123
00:41:49,642 --> 00:41:51,610
- [Crow] This!
This is the matter!

1124
00:41:51,643 --> 00:41:54,213
(loud zinging)

1125
00:41:56,015 --> 00:41:58,583
- [Servo] The pilot is teething!

1126
00:42:00,285 --> 00:42:01,720
- [Munakata] A dragon ship!

1127
00:42:01,753 --> 00:42:03,288
A black dragon!

1128
00:42:03,322 --> 00:42:04,257
- What?

1129
00:42:04,290 --> 00:42:05,323
- [Servo] What do you mean what?

1130
00:42:05,357 --> 00:42:08,260
- Munakata, what did you say?

1131
00:42:08,293 --> 00:42:09,628
(Munakata shouts)

1132
00:42:09,662 --> 00:42:11,763
- [Crow] I hit my
knee on the dashboard!

1133
00:42:11,797 --> 00:42:12,732
Wow! Hurts!

1134
00:42:14,733 --> 00:42:16,068
- [Servo] There is dog
hair all over the car!

1135
00:42:16,102 --> 00:42:17,737
Why do you think that is, hm?

1136
00:42:17,770 --> 00:42:19,805
- Oh, good evening, Professor!

1137
00:42:19,838 --> 00:42:21,407
- [Professor] Good evening!

1138
00:42:21,440 --> 00:42:23,175
- And then all the notes
that you asked me to take

1139
00:42:23,208 --> 00:42:24,910
at the conference last week.

1140
00:42:24,943 --> 00:42:27,378
I'm sure you'll find
everything in order, Doctor.

1141
00:42:27,412 --> 00:42:29,113
- Oh, if you did
it, I'm sure I will!

1142
00:42:29,147 --> 00:42:30,415
- Thank you, sir.

1143
00:42:30,415 --> 00:42:32,183
- Hey, Dad, Dad, wait!

1144
00:42:32,217 --> 00:42:33,252
Wait, Dad!

1145
00:42:33,285 --> 00:42:34,620
- Secretary of children.
- Oh, John!

1146
00:42:34,653 --> 00:42:36,255
Did you have a good
day at school, son?

1147
00:42:36,288 --> 00:42:37,088
- Yes, I did.

1148
00:42:37,122 --> 00:42:37,957
I wanted to talk to you.

1149
00:42:37,990 --> 00:42:39,458
Where are you going?

1150
00:42:39,492 --> 00:42:41,160
- To the Defense Ministry.
- Will you be back soon?

1151
00:42:41,193 --> 00:42:42,427
- [Servo] No,
because I loathe you!

1152
00:42:42,460 --> 00:42:44,297
- Not before your
bedtime, I'm afraid.

1153
00:42:44,330 --> 00:42:46,298
- Aww gee, Dad.

1154
00:42:46,332 --> 00:42:48,200
I want to talk to you!

1155
00:42:48,233 --> 00:42:50,402
About these invaders
from outer space.

1156
00:42:50,435 --> 00:42:52,003
- [Crow] He's putting
his cigarette out on him!

1157
00:42:52,037 --> 00:42:53,605
Ow!

1158
00:42:53,638 --> 00:42:55,107
- Well, let's talk about
it tomorrow morning

1159
00:42:55,140 --> 00:42:56,642
at breakfast, huh?

1160
00:42:57,810 --> 00:42:59,412
- [Crow] Um, how come
you're so old, Dad?

1161
00:42:59,445 --> 00:43:02,447
Did you have me when you
were like 60 or something?

1162
00:43:02,480 --> 00:43:04,417
- Oh, I'm afraid I'm a bit
late for this conference.

1163
00:43:04,450 --> 00:43:06,118
Major Murkey will be worried.

1164
00:43:06,152 --> 00:43:07,585
Will you call him and
tell him I'm on my way?

1165
00:43:07,620 --> 00:43:09,355
- Certainly, goodbye, Doctor!

1166
00:43:09,388 --> 00:43:10,788
- Bye, Dad!

1167
00:43:10,822 --> 00:43:12,625
And don't forget our theory!

1168
00:43:12,658 --> 00:43:15,293
- [Servo] Goodbye, people I
seem to share a house with!

1169
00:43:15,327 --> 00:43:18,663
(engine growls)

1170
00:43:18,697 --> 00:43:20,365
- [Crow] Goodbye.

1171
00:43:20,398 --> 00:43:23,302
- I'm sorry, Dr. Macken
has not yet arrived.

1172
00:43:23,335 --> 00:43:26,172
- But, Major, what could
have happened to him?

1173
00:43:26,205 --> 00:43:27,605
It's not like Macken at all

1174
00:43:27,640 --> 00:43:29,408
to be this late
for an appointment.

1175
00:43:29,442 --> 00:43:31,077
- Gentlemen, I'm quite
alarmed about this.

1176
00:43:31,110 --> 00:43:32,577
Dr. Macken may be in trouble.

1177
00:43:32,610 --> 00:43:34,713
In any case, we can do
nothing without him.

1178
00:43:34,747 --> 00:43:37,548
At least may be able to
determine his whereabouts.

1179
00:43:37,548 --> 00:43:38,550
Major Murkey,

1180
00:43:38,583 --> 00:43:40,018
with your permission--
- Murky?

1181
00:43:40,052 --> 00:43:41,387
- This matter immediately.
- Very good, Captain.

1182
00:43:41,420 --> 00:43:42,253
Go ahead.

1183
00:43:43,455 --> 00:43:45,757
Gentlemen, I suggest
a half hour recess--

1184
00:43:45,790 --> 00:43:47,893
- Recess!
- Woohoo!

1185
00:43:47,927 --> 00:43:50,562
(wind howls)
- Wow!

1186
00:43:50,595 --> 00:43:53,832
The Earth is so smooth, it
must have been dermabrasioned!

1187
00:43:53,865 --> 00:43:56,702
(wind howls)

1188
00:43:56,735 --> 00:43:59,705
- [Crow] Sounds like the
Earth needs new break pads.

1189
00:43:59,738 --> 00:44:01,207
See how things are goin'.

1190
00:44:01,240 --> 00:44:04,075
- [Mike] Okay,
we'll check it out.

1191
00:44:08,547 --> 00:44:11,583
("MST3K Love Theme")

1192
00:44:14,987 --> 00:44:16,455
- Yep, seems like it doesn't it?

1193
00:44:16,488 --> 00:44:18,590
- So you think we're back in
sync on the whole time thing?

1194
00:44:18,623 --> 00:44:19,792
(Tom chuckles)
- D'oh!

1195
00:44:19,825 --> 00:44:20,958
- Oh, I'm sorry, sorry--

1196
00:44:20,992 --> 00:44:22,493
- Okay, hey guys, listen up.

1197
00:44:22,527 --> 00:44:23,895
I think I have some answers.

1198
00:44:23,928 --> 00:44:25,630
Apparently, the
separate universe layers

1199
00:44:25,663 --> 00:44:27,098
are co-mingling.
(Tom laughs)

1200
00:44:27,132 --> 00:44:29,100
If we don't isolate our
position in space and time,

1201
00:44:29,133 --> 00:44:31,737
(robots laugh)
limitless potential--

1202
00:44:31,770 --> 00:44:32,905
What?

1203
00:44:32,938 --> 00:44:34,740
- Mike, you're a small robot!
- Yeah!

1204
00:44:34,773 --> 00:44:36,708
- (laughs) Of course, I am!

1205
00:44:36,742 --> 00:44:38,243
What do you expect?

1206
00:44:38,277 --> 00:44:39,778
- Well, normally when we're
not in a wormhole and stuff,

1207
00:44:39,812 --> 00:44:42,113
you're a big,
chunky human thing!

1208
00:44:42,147 --> 00:44:43,948
- Well, I don't mean to
offend you or anything

1209
00:44:43,948 --> 00:44:46,017
but as you are, I have
the urge to put you back

1210
00:44:46,052 --> 00:44:47,920
in your cage!
(robots laugh)

1211
00:44:47,953 --> 00:44:49,388
- C'mon, cut it out.

1212
00:44:49,422 --> 00:44:51,022
Now, I can't speak for
your reality but in mine,

1213
00:44:51,057 --> 00:44:53,958
we are all robots serving on
this vessel and I'm in command.

1214
00:44:53,992 --> 00:44:55,760
You have tremendous
respect for me!

1215
00:44:55,793 --> 00:44:56,695
You do!

1216
00:44:56,728 --> 00:44:57,963
Now my orders are as follows.

1217
00:44:57,997 --> 00:44:59,197
I want you--
- Sorry, Mike.

1218
00:44:59,230 --> 00:45:00,932
I only take orders
from Willy Tyler

1219
00:45:00,965 --> 00:45:03,002
and Lester Hog!
- Oho, good one!

1220
00:45:03,035 --> 00:45:03,868
(robots laugh)
- Oh, that's--

1221
00:45:03,902 --> 00:45:04,903
Stop, now come on, stop!

1222
00:45:04,937 --> 00:45:05,737
Now stop it!

1223
00:45:05,770 --> 00:45:06,872
Now listen up!

1224
00:45:06,905 --> 00:45:07,672
We all wanna get back right?
- Yes.

1225
00:45:07,705 --> 00:45:09,107
- Okay, listen up.

1226
00:45:09,140 --> 00:45:11,343
If we wanna put things right,
you'll do just as I say.

1227
00:45:11,377 --> 00:45:13,445
If we can overdrive
the plasma thrusters

1228
00:45:13,478 --> 00:45:14,847
to create a gravity well,

1229
00:45:14,880 --> 00:45:16,815
isolating us from the
other universe layers,

1230
00:45:16,815 --> 00:45:19,752
we untangle our co-mingling--
(robots laugh loudly)

1231
00:45:19,785 --> 00:45:21,953
- He's so cute!
- Come on, cut it out!

1232
00:45:21,987 --> 00:45:24,055
You guys are gonna be
annihilated and stuff!

1233
00:45:24,088 --> 00:45:25,290
- Oh, Mike, I don't care, man!

1234
00:45:25,323 --> 00:45:26,592
It's worth it to
see you like this!

1235
00:45:26,625 --> 00:45:28,227
- No, stop it!
(loud buzzing)

1236
00:45:28,260 --> 00:45:29,928
(Mike and robots
shout indistinctly)

1237
00:45:29,962 --> 00:45:33,465
- [Mike] Don't push, don't
push, don't push, don't push!

1238
00:45:33,498 --> 00:45:36,468
(doors open loudly)

1239
00:45:44,008 --> 00:45:45,410
- [Crow] Come on,
move it, Short Stuff!

1240
00:45:45,443 --> 00:45:49,413
- [Mike] I'm movin', I'm
movin', don't push, I'm fine.

1241
00:45:50,715 --> 00:45:51,617
- [Crow] It says
employees must wash hands

1242
00:45:51,650 --> 00:45:52,785
before returning to invasion!

1243
00:45:52,818 --> 00:45:55,553
(Mike chuckles)

1244
00:45:57,322 --> 00:46:01,493
- [Mike] (gasps) A
mummified Alf Landon!

1245
00:46:04,930 --> 00:46:06,298
- [Servo] Good morning, honey!

1246
00:46:06,332 --> 00:46:07,800
- Professor Macken.

1247
00:46:07,833 --> 00:46:09,702
Welcome aboard.

1248
00:46:09,735 --> 00:46:10,868
- Who, who are you?

1249
00:46:10,902 --> 00:46:11,937
- Come, come, Professor!

1250
00:46:11,970 --> 00:46:13,972
Permit me to introduce myself!

1251
00:46:14,005 --> 00:46:16,308
They call me Phantom

1252
00:46:16,342 --> 00:46:17,275
of Krankor.

1253
00:46:18,343 --> 00:46:19,712
But you seem
startled, Professor.

1254
00:46:19,745 --> 00:46:21,480
Sit down, relax.

1255
00:46:21,513 --> 00:46:24,717
- [Crow] Hey, Z-7, suck it in!

1256
00:46:24,750 --> 00:46:26,518
- Is this a dream?

1257
00:46:26,552 --> 00:46:27,853
Where am I?

1258
00:46:27,887 --> 00:46:29,287
- You want to know
where you are?

1259
00:46:29,320 --> 00:46:30,522
- [Servo] No, I
wanna know (mumbles).

1260
00:46:30,555 --> 00:46:31,957
Of course I wanna
know where I am!

1261
00:46:31,990 --> 00:46:34,325
- Aboard my flagship.

1262
00:46:34,358 --> 00:46:37,595
Halfway between your
world and Krankor.

1263
00:46:38,730 --> 00:46:40,965
- [Professor] How did
you bring me here?

1264
00:46:40,998 --> 00:46:42,433
- For a man of
your intelligence,

1265
00:46:42,467 --> 00:46:45,037
a full explanation
would be necessary.

1266
00:46:45,070 --> 00:46:47,973
But we have no time
for that, Professor.

1267
00:46:48,007 --> 00:46:49,575
- But what about my chauffer?

1268
00:46:49,608 --> 00:46:53,278
- Come now, my dear Professor,
what a silly question!

1269
00:46:53,312 --> 00:46:56,882
Do you expect me to keep track
of your worthless servants?

1270
00:46:56,882 --> 00:46:58,617
We blasted him
out of an airlock,

1271
00:46:58,650 --> 00:47:02,820
so by now he may have fallen
into a star! (laughs evilly)

1272
00:47:05,057 --> 00:47:06,458
- [Servo] Wow,
that guy's nuttier

1273
00:47:06,492 --> 00:47:09,595
than a Stuckey's log.
- Well, I suppose

1274
00:47:09,628 --> 00:47:12,430
that you expect me to help
you with your evil plans!

1275
00:47:12,463 --> 00:47:13,498
- [Crow] Yeah, would you mind?

1276
00:47:13,532 --> 00:47:14,733
Thanks!
- That is precisely

1277
00:47:14,767 --> 00:47:17,102
why I gave orders
to take you aboard.

1278
00:47:17,135 --> 00:47:20,505
I will show you much here
that only you can appreciate.

1279
00:47:20,538 --> 00:47:24,142
For example how I propose
to control the universe!

1280
00:47:24,175 --> 00:47:26,110
When you've seen all this,

1281
00:47:26,143 --> 00:47:28,447
you will realize
how futile it is

1282
00:47:28,480 --> 00:47:30,848
for you or anyone
else to oppose me!

1283
00:47:30,848 --> 00:47:34,452
- [Servo] Fine, just
go light on the probes!

1284
00:47:34,485 --> 00:47:37,488
(loud zinging)
Making no progress at all.

1285
00:47:37,522 --> 00:47:38,923
- [Crow] It's incredible
how accurate this is

1286
00:47:38,957 --> 00:47:40,558
at depicting space!

1287
00:47:42,627 --> 00:47:46,798
♪ Some people call me
Space Cowboy, yeah ♪

1288
00:47:48,567 --> 00:47:49,367
- Hey!

1289
00:47:49,400 --> 00:47:50,568
Look at that!

1290
00:47:50,602 --> 00:47:53,572
- [Mike] Oh, oh, I'm
sorry, I got distracted.

1291
00:47:53,605 --> 00:47:55,107
- Oh!

1292
00:47:55,140 --> 00:47:58,310
- [Crow] There's the kids'
playroom and we're gonna--

1293
00:47:58,343 --> 00:47:59,578
- Hey, Chief, we got
that flying saucer

1294
00:47:59,612 --> 00:48:00,412
on the televisers.

1295
00:48:00,445 --> 00:48:01,713
Coming up fast at stern!

1296
00:48:01,747 --> 00:48:02,813
- What?

1297
00:48:02,813 --> 00:48:04,448
- [Servo] What?

1298
00:48:04,482 --> 00:48:05,950
- Get him back to his
quarters under guard!

1299
00:48:05,983 --> 00:48:07,318
- [Henchman] Right, sir.

1300
00:48:07,352 --> 00:48:08,153
Come on, you.

1301
00:48:08,187 --> 00:48:09,788
- [Mike] Oh, speed! Oh!

1302
00:48:09,822 --> 00:48:11,590
- Come on, I said!

1303
00:48:11,623 --> 00:48:14,325
- [Crow] It's the
instant miso soup bower!

1304
00:48:14,358 --> 00:48:18,363
(Mike hums Pop Goes the Weasel)

1305
00:48:20,565 --> 00:48:22,467
- Eh, it's him alright.

1306
00:48:23,902 --> 00:48:26,705
- [Mike] Saying it is me
will have no effect on me.

1307
00:48:26,738 --> 00:48:28,673
(loud whooshing)

1308
00:48:28,707 --> 00:48:31,843
- [Crow] It's a flying
rotary nose hair clipper!

1309
00:48:31,877 --> 00:48:33,012
- I've got him right
where I want him!

1310
00:48:33,045 --> 00:48:35,747
- [Servo] Somewhere in space!

1311
00:48:35,780 --> 00:48:36,882
- [Mike] Don't look at my butt!

1312
00:48:36,915 --> 00:48:38,083
- Now he dies!

1313
00:48:39,517 --> 00:48:41,820
- [Crow] Just wanna test
some batteries here first!

1314
00:48:41,853 --> 00:48:43,888
(loud zinging)

1315
00:48:43,922 --> 00:48:48,060
- [Servo] Aha, and they
stay crunchy in milk, hmm!

1316
00:48:49,260 --> 00:48:52,530
- [Mike] Swing me over
there, trusty string!

1317
00:48:53,698 --> 00:48:55,967
- [Crow] He's in
the wiener mobile!

1318
00:48:56,000 --> 00:48:57,468
(loud zinging)

1319
00:48:57,502 --> 00:49:01,573
- [Servo] Oh no, he lost
control of his fried egg!

1320
00:49:03,442 --> 00:49:04,275
- Enough.

1321
00:49:05,243 --> 00:49:06,345
He's finished.

1322
00:49:06,378 --> 00:49:08,013
- [Mike] Look at that.

1323
00:49:08,047 --> 00:49:10,048
- [Servo] Oh! No, don't!

1324
00:49:11,950 --> 00:49:13,618
(evil laugh)

1325
00:49:13,652 --> 00:49:17,688
- [Mike] I have to tell
Fang about that! Ha!

1326
00:49:17,722 --> 00:49:19,323
(loud zing)
- They're landing

1327
00:49:19,357 --> 00:49:21,427
on Captain Picard's head!

1328
00:49:23,228 --> 00:49:24,963
- [Servo] Oh, it's a planet
where sea monkeys come from!

1329
00:49:24,997 --> 00:49:26,498
(Mike chuckles)

1330
00:49:26,532 --> 00:49:28,900
(loud zing)

1331
00:49:28,933 --> 00:49:30,568
- [Crow] Whoa! Look at that!

1332
00:49:30,602 --> 00:49:31,803
Look at that!

1333
00:49:31,837 --> 00:49:33,105
- [Servo] It's a trip
to Mike's subconscious!

1334
00:49:33,138 --> 00:49:35,973
- [Mike] It's pretty
accurate, I gotta admit.

1335
00:49:36,007 --> 00:49:38,343
- [Crow] It's a DQ planet!

1336
00:49:38,377 --> 00:49:40,078
(loud zing)
(loud whir)

1337
00:49:40,112 --> 00:49:43,782
- [Servo] Dress to
the right stuff!

1338
00:49:43,782 --> 00:49:45,883
- Chafe, chafe,
chafe, chafe, chafe.

1339
00:49:45,917 --> 00:49:47,518
- Shall I put Macken
with the others?

1340
00:49:47,552 --> 00:49:49,120
- Of course not.

1341
00:49:49,153 --> 00:49:50,222
Bring him to the great hall.

1342
00:49:50,255 --> 00:49:51,423
- Right, sir.

1343
00:49:51,457 --> 00:49:52,690
- And prepare to
return to Earth.

1344
00:49:52,723 --> 00:49:54,192
- Right, sir!

1345
00:49:54,225 --> 00:49:57,262
- [Mike] Uh, didn't we just
get back from Earth, sir?

1346
00:49:57,295 --> 00:50:00,132
- [Servo] Sir, do
we have a plan or--

1347
00:50:00,165 --> 00:50:02,167
- [Crow] So, crack corn
all around then, gentlemen?

1348
00:50:02,200 --> 00:50:03,935
- I've a special job for you!
- Yes, sir!

1349
00:50:03,968 --> 00:50:05,903
- I want you to find
that Prince of Space.

1350
00:50:05,937 --> 00:50:07,005
- Prince of Space?

1351
00:50:07,038 --> 00:50:08,773
- You heard me right.

1352
00:50:08,807 --> 00:50:10,508
He may have possibly
escaped destruction

1353
00:50:10,542 --> 00:50:12,477
when we passed through
that meteorite shower.

1354
00:50:12,510 --> 00:50:13,945
- [Servo] Prince of Space, sir?

1355
00:50:13,978 --> 00:50:16,347
- I must have positive
proof that he's finished.

1356
00:50:16,382 --> 00:50:19,483
He may make some foolish
attempt to rescue our prisoners

1357
00:50:19,517 --> 00:50:21,920
and disrupt my
plans for the Earth.

1358
00:50:21,953 --> 00:50:23,222
- [Mike] Uh, sir,
I was gonna ask you

1359
00:50:23,255 --> 00:50:25,257
if I should bring this
to the lab, don't! Oh!

1360
00:50:25,290 --> 00:50:26,525
- The last we saw of his ship,

1361
00:50:26,558 --> 00:50:28,025
it was falling
away toward Earth.

1362
00:50:28,060 --> 00:50:30,295
He may possibly have been
able to return to his base!

1363
00:50:30,328 --> 00:50:31,997
- [Crow] Prince of Space?

1364
00:50:32,030 --> 00:50:33,698
- [Henchman] Of course, he
must have a base somewhere!

1365
00:50:33,732 --> 00:50:35,200
- That's right.

1366
00:50:35,233 --> 00:50:37,735
He must have one there
and I want you to find it.

1367
00:50:37,768 --> 00:50:38,870
- I'll find it alright.

1368
00:50:38,903 --> 00:50:40,172
I can promise you that!

1369
00:50:40,205 --> 00:50:41,607
- You'd better take
the X-radar with you

1370
00:50:41,640 --> 00:50:43,208
to help you find him!

1371
00:50:43,242 --> 00:50:46,878
He sure will give you the
formula for his wavelength.

1372
00:50:46,912 --> 00:50:47,878
You.
- Fight me!

1373
00:50:47,912 --> 00:50:50,115
- Accompany him!
- Right, sir!

1374
00:50:50,148 --> 00:50:52,583
- Install the X-radar in
one of the ground cars

1375
00:50:52,617 --> 00:50:56,422
of the Earthlings and
comb the city for him!

1376
00:50:56,455 --> 00:50:57,588
(Mike and robots snicker)

1377
00:50:57,622 --> 00:50:58,990
He's bound to be
disguised, of course.

1378
00:50:59,023 --> 00:51:00,358
Perhaps as a civilian.

1379
00:51:00,392 --> 00:51:01,593
But if it's properly set up,

1380
00:51:01,627 --> 00:51:03,828
the X-radar will
find him easily!

1381
00:51:03,862 --> 00:51:06,532
And when you find
him, report to me!

1382
00:51:06,565 --> 00:51:08,867
And above all,
keep track of him.

1383
00:51:08,900 --> 00:51:12,103
I prefer to deal
personally with him.

1384
00:51:12,137 --> 00:51:14,672
And if you don't find him,
don't bother to come back!

1385
00:51:14,705 --> 00:51:15,607
- [Henchmen] Right, sir!

1386
00:51:15,640 --> 00:51:17,375
We go to obey your orders!

1387
00:51:17,408 --> 00:51:18,610
- Dismissed!

1388
00:51:18,643 --> 00:51:20,012
- [Servo] First, we have
to go to the bathroom!

1389
00:51:20,045 --> 00:51:21,547
(loud buzz)
- Professor Macken is waiting

1390
00:51:21,580 --> 00:51:22,980
for you in the great hall!

1391
00:51:23,013 --> 00:51:25,050
- [Crow] Always quarter to
three here at Krankor's place!

1392
00:51:25,083 --> 00:51:25,883
- Good.

1393
00:51:28,387 --> 00:51:29,620
You.

1394
00:51:29,653 --> 00:51:30,988
Bring in the others and
put 'em up on the stage.

1395
00:51:31,055 --> 00:51:32,523
- Yes, sir.

1396
00:51:32,557 --> 00:51:35,727
- I'm ashamed of my talk show.
(Mike laughs)

1397
00:51:35,760 --> 00:51:39,430
- [Crow] Great hall designed
by the Lego Corporation!

1398
00:51:39,463 --> 00:51:41,032
- [Servo] Well, we don't
have as big a turnout

1399
00:51:41,065 --> 00:51:43,235
as we expected tonight so if
you could all just move down

1400
00:51:43,268 --> 00:51:45,137
to the first few rows...

1401
00:51:45,170 --> 00:51:48,072
- At ease, men.
- I mean, man.

1402
00:51:48,105 --> 00:51:50,342
- Professor Macken.

1403
00:51:50,375 --> 00:51:51,477
- (snorts) Oh, ah, oh!
- I want to bid you welcome

1404
00:51:51,510 --> 00:51:53,712
to the planet of Krankor!

1405
00:51:53,745 --> 00:51:55,013
And to my home.

1406
00:51:56,447 --> 00:51:59,885
You must have seen a lot from
the window of my flagship.

1407
00:51:59,918 --> 00:52:02,387
The castle cut from
the living rock.

1408
00:52:02,420 --> 00:52:05,423
My giant guardian and so forth.

1409
00:52:05,457 --> 00:52:08,627
I have many more
wonders to show you.

1410
00:52:08,660 --> 00:52:10,862
And I've even brought
some friends of yours

1411
00:52:10,895 --> 00:52:13,198
to share this
experience with you!

1412
00:52:13,232 --> 00:52:16,433
- [Crow] Can I get more
coffee over here, please?

1413
00:52:16,467 --> 00:52:19,037
- [Servo] Pork and Mr. Moonies.

1414
00:52:20,272 --> 00:52:21,740
- [Mike] All my roadie friends!

1415
00:52:21,773 --> 00:52:22,873
- Dr. Fletcher!

1416
00:52:22,907 --> 00:52:24,042
- Oh!

1417
00:52:24,075 --> 00:52:25,010
Macken!

1418
00:52:25,043 --> 00:52:26,410
- [Crow] I'm scared!

1419
00:52:26,443 --> 00:52:27,312
- Are you alright?

1420
00:52:27,345 --> 00:52:28,547
- Oh, Professor!

1421
00:52:28,580 --> 00:52:32,183
- [Mike] I forgot to
water your plants!

1422
00:52:32,217 --> 00:52:33,652
- [Mike And Robots] Lucille!

1423
00:52:33,685 --> 00:52:35,153
- Dr. Cummings!

1424
00:52:35,187 --> 00:52:37,188
- [Dr. Fletcher] Yes, and
this is Professor Coin.

1425
00:52:37,222 --> 00:52:38,690
- Lucille.
- Oh, I'm so sorry

1426
00:52:38,723 --> 00:52:40,258
about this, Dr. Cummings.

1427
00:52:40,292 --> 00:52:41,893
- [Dr. Fletcher] And
here is Professor Goriets

1428
00:52:41,927 --> 00:52:43,328
from Southern Institute.

1429
00:52:43,362 --> 00:52:44,595
- Lucille.
- Oh.

1430
00:52:47,998 --> 00:52:49,533
- [Servo] Mrs. Karma Goat.

1431
00:52:49,567 --> 00:52:52,803
- [Phantom] Gentlemen,
we have much to discuss!

1432
00:52:52,837 --> 00:52:54,138
Please sit down!

1433
00:52:55,007 --> 00:52:56,140
- [Crow] Please.

1434
00:52:56,173 --> 00:52:57,742
No, really, please!

1435
00:52:57,775 --> 00:52:58,610
Sit down!

1436
00:52:59,677 --> 00:53:00,578
- [Servo] So
they're alien except

1437
00:53:00,612 --> 00:53:02,847
for their Chippendale furniture.

1438
00:53:02,847 --> 00:53:05,883
- [Mike] Sorry, I'm late, cat
threw up this morning, hi.

1439
00:53:05,917 --> 00:53:07,552
- Very good.
- You sit well!

1440
00:53:07,585 --> 00:53:09,888
- Everyone I need
seems to be here.

1441
00:53:09,922 --> 00:53:12,890
I appreciate your
coming, gentlemen.

1442
00:53:12,923 --> 00:53:15,327
I'm honored to find
myself in the company

1443
00:53:15,360 --> 00:53:18,463
of five of the most
advanced minds of Earth.

1444
00:53:18,497 --> 00:53:20,365
Please make yourselves
comfortable.

1445
00:53:20,398 --> 00:53:23,335
- Until they arrive.
- While I explain my plans.

1446
00:53:23,368 --> 00:53:26,938
Plans in which you gentlemen
play a very important part.

1447
00:53:26,972 --> 00:53:30,142
(laughs evilly)
- I have to leave early.

1448
00:53:30,175 --> 00:53:31,977
- [Doctor] You can't!
This is impossible!

1449
00:53:32,010 --> 00:53:33,645
- Be silent.

1450
00:53:33,678 --> 00:53:35,780
I am dictator of Krankor.

1451
00:53:36,715 --> 00:53:38,215
I assure you

1452
00:53:38,250 --> 00:53:40,585
that the word impossible

1453
00:53:40,618 --> 00:53:43,355
is a word, which for
me, does not exist.

1454
00:53:43,388 --> 00:53:44,822
- [Crow] Although
I just said it.

1455
00:53:44,855 --> 00:53:47,292
- [Phantom] Now, first
of all, Professor Macken.

1456
00:53:47,325 --> 00:53:49,727
I've arranged an
interesting show for you.

1457
00:53:49,760 --> 00:53:53,532
I trust that you will
find it quite instructive!

1458
00:53:53,565 --> 00:53:57,135
Go ahead.
(Tom hums loudly)

1459
00:53:59,703 --> 00:54:01,538
- [Mike] Lean forward.

1460
00:54:04,408 --> 00:54:05,510
- Why, that--

1461
00:54:06,712 --> 00:54:08,280
Why, that's my house!

1462
00:54:08,313 --> 00:54:09,480
- So it is.

1463
00:54:09,513 --> 00:54:11,650
You are quite right,
Professor Macken.

1464
00:54:11,683 --> 00:54:12,650
Your house.

1465
00:54:12,683 --> 00:54:14,118
- [Servo] You win this round.

1466
00:54:14,152 --> 00:54:16,587
- And it's half a million
Earth miles from here.

1467
00:54:16,622 --> 00:54:20,392
- [Mike] But it's
on the bus line...

1468
00:54:20,425 --> 00:54:21,525
- Oh!

1469
00:54:21,558 --> 00:54:22,793
Johnnie!

1470
00:54:22,827 --> 00:54:24,095
- [Crow] The slammed
the iron gate on me

1471
00:54:24,128 --> 00:54:26,563
at cram school again today!

1472
00:54:26,597 --> 00:54:29,968
(melancholy music)

1473
00:54:30,002 --> 00:54:31,402
- [Servo] Samuel Barbers' adagio

1474
00:54:31,435 --> 00:54:33,772
for young Japanese children.

1475
00:54:35,673 --> 00:54:37,675
- [Mike] (chuckles) That's cold.

1476
00:54:37,708 --> 00:54:39,043
- [Crow] Well, I'm
sure this little scene

1477
00:54:39,077 --> 00:54:41,545
is leading somewhere if
you'll all be patient.

1478
00:54:41,578 --> 00:54:43,147
- [Servo] Now watch as we
turn the lawn sprinklers

1479
00:54:43,180 --> 00:54:44,983
on our little Johnnie!

1480
00:54:46,317 --> 00:54:50,122
- [Mike] Here's the
Japanese Suzanne Pleshette.

1481
00:54:50,722 --> 00:54:53,157
(loud zinging)

1482
00:54:53,190 --> 00:54:56,527
- [Crow] Jeez, my
life is really boring!

1483
00:54:58,597 --> 00:55:00,432
- [Phantom] Well, gentlemen,
what do you think of that?

1484
00:55:00,465 --> 00:55:01,298
- [Servo] What?

1485
00:55:01,332 --> 00:55:02,800
I just got better.

1486
00:55:02,833 --> 00:55:04,802
- [Phantom] Nothing you do on
Earth can be hidden from me!

1487
00:55:04,835 --> 00:55:06,872
I've watched all of
your secrets from here!

1488
00:55:06,905 --> 00:55:09,340
You see, I've been watching
you for a long time now.

1489
00:55:09,373 --> 00:55:10,575
- [Mike] He knows
about the porn.

1490
00:55:10,608 --> 00:55:12,110
- [Phantom] And I knew
right where to find you

1491
00:55:12,143 --> 00:55:13,345
when I wanted to.

1492
00:55:13,378 --> 00:55:14,978
- [Crow] So you
know about my rash?!

1493
00:55:15,013 --> 00:55:16,580
- That's an impressive
toy but first of all,

1494
00:55:16,580 --> 00:55:18,148
I demand to know why
you brought us here!

1495
00:55:18,182 --> 00:55:19,450
- [Servo] Grab some bed, flumpy!

1496
00:55:19,483 --> 00:55:20,885
- You demand nothing.

1497
00:55:20,918 --> 00:55:23,622
You will merely obey
my instructions.

1498
00:55:23,655 --> 00:55:26,090
Take your place
and remain silent

1499
00:55:26,123 --> 00:55:29,527
while I explain why
you were brought here.

1500
00:55:29,560 --> 00:55:33,498
You five men are among the
top scientists of Earth.

1501
00:55:33,532 --> 00:55:35,733
Your governments
respect your opinions,

1502
00:55:35,767 --> 00:55:39,237
thus, you men are well
equipped to evaluate my power!

1503
00:55:39,270 --> 00:55:42,773
You know I can exterminate
the world any time I want to.

1504
00:55:42,807 --> 00:55:44,875
I want you to explain
this to your people.

1505
00:55:44,908 --> 00:55:48,112
Impress upon them how useless
it would be to oppose me!

1506
00:55:48,145 --> 00:55:50,948
You will tell them I
demand their surrender.

1507
00:55:50,982 --> 00:55:52,283
You.
- Bite me!

1508
00:55:52,317 --> 00:55:54,185
- You, each and
every one of you!

1509
00:55:54,218 --> 00:55:55,620
- Bite me!
- No! I won't!

1510
00:55:55,653 --> 00:55:56,822
It's out of the question!

1511
00:55:56,855 --> 00:55:58,155
I won't!

1512
00:55:58,188 --> 00:55:59,790
I will never betray my people!

1513
00:55:59,823 --> 00:56:01,860
- I refuse categorically--
- No, I will never

1514
00:56:01,893 --> 00:56:02,793
be your tool!

1515
00:56:02,827 --> 00:56:03,628
- [Doctor] None of us will!

1516
00:56:03,662 --> 00:56:04,762
- Agreed!

1517
00:56:04,795 --> 00:56:06,463
- Of course we agree!

1518
00:56:06,497 --> 00:56:07,632
- [Servo] I'll do it!

1519
00:56:07,665 --> 00:56:09,767
- Apparently you
gentlemen are upset.

1520
00:56:09,800 --> 00:56:11,635
I will give you a
chance to think it over.

1521
00:56:11,668 --> 00:56:12,870
Calmly.

1522
00:56:12,903 --> 00:56:14,638
After all you are
men of science.

1523
00:56:14,672 --> 00:56:17,075
We are leaving to attack
your world in 12 hours.

1524
00:56:17,108 --> 00:56:18,175
- What's he going to do?

1525
00:56:18,208 --> 00:56:20,278
- With your cooperation
or without it,

1526
00:56:20,312 --> 00:56:22,080
I'm going to attack.

1527
00:56:22,113 --> 00:56:24,948
I shall destroy one of
your major cities first.

1528
00:56:24,982 --> 00:56:27,385
Afterward, I'm sure
you will cooperate.

1529
00:56:27,418 --> 00:56:29,353
(laughs evilly)

1530
00:56:29,387 --> 00:56:30,455
- [Servo] Starts with the
United (mumbles) is it?

1531
00:56:30,488 --> 00:56:31,823
- [Mike] No.

1532
00:56:31,857 --> 00:56:33,458
- [Crow] The young one ship.

1533
00:56:33,492 --> 00:56:35,793
(loud zing)

1534
00:56:37,362 --> 00:56:38,430
It's kinda hard to
go into warp drive

1535
00:56:38,463 --> 00:56:40,332
when you're burnin' so much oil.

1536
00:56:40,365 --> 00:56:42,533
- Professor, may I?
- Thank you.

1537
00:56:42,567 --> 00:56:44,102
- You must eat something!

1538
00:56:44,135 --> 00:56:45,337
Do you feel alright?

1539
00:56:45,370 --> 00:56:48,272
- [Servo] Don't light a
match is all I'll say!

1540
00:56:48,305 --> 00:56:49,740
- The poor man suffers so.

1541
00:56:49,773 --> 00:56:50,875
- [Crow] I'm from
the 19th century,

1542
00:56:50,908 --> 00:56:53,210
what does he want with me?

1543
00:56:53,243 --> 00:56:54,912
- [Mike] Bad news, all
out of curly fries.

1544
00:56:54,945 --> 00:56:55,847
- The Chief wants you.

1545
00:56:55,880 --> 00:56:57,282
- [Mike] In the worst way!

1546
00:56:57,315 --> 00:56:58,717
- [Professor] We were just
about to begin eating.

1547
00:56:58,750 --> 00:57:00,785
- You eat later.
- And me.

1548
00:57:04,355 --> 00:57:05,523
- What's the matter?

1549
00:57:05,557 --> 00:57:07,425
Isn't our food good
enough for you?

1550
00:57:07,458 --> 00:57:10,328
Come on, hurry up with you!

1551
00:57:10,362 --> 00:57:11,262
- [Professor] The man is sick!

1552
00:57:11,295 --> 00:57:12,597
Leave him alone!

1553
00:57:12,630 --> 00:57:14,632
- On your feet, you!
- But he's a sick man!

1554
00:57:14,665 --> 00:57:15,900
- Get away!

1555
00:57:15,933 --> 00:57:16,968
- [Crow] Oh, he waved
his stinky foot at me!

1556
00:57:17,002 --> 00:57:18,837
- [Henchman] Come on, eat this!

1557
00:57:18,870 --> 00:57:20,438
Eat it, I tell you!

1558
00:57:21,372 --> 00:57:23,207
- [Mike] Ah, Mr. Bond.

1559
00:57:23,240 --> 00:57:25,543
- Ah, good morning, gentlemen.

1560
00:57:25,577 --> 00:57:27,378
You slept well, I hope.

1561
00:57:27,412 --> 00:57:28,378
- [Servo] Yes, in
my double-breasted

1562
00:57:28,412 --> 00:57:30,448
sleeping suit and tie.

1563
00:57:30,515 --> 00:57:32,217
- [Mike] Tell Mom
we're about to eat.

1564
00:57:32,250 --> 00:57:33,618
- [Doctor] Listen.

1565
00:57:33,652 --> 00:57:35,720
I speak for my colleagues
as well as myself.

1566
00:57:35,753 --> 00:57:38,122
It is impossible to
agree to your demands.

1567
00:57:38,155 --> 00:57:39,357
- What?

1568
00:57:39,390 --> 00:57:40,925
- [Doctor] We are
only men of science.

1569
00:57:40,958 --> 00:57:43,495
We can explain to our people
the state of your technology.

1570
00:57:43,528 --> 00:57:44,928
But we cannot accept
responsibility

1571
00:57:44,962 --> 00:57:46,430
for making political decisions.

1572
00:57:46,463 --> 00:57:47,765
- [Crow] Who's talking?

1573
00:57:47,798 --> 00:57:48,933
(Mike chuckles)
- Again!

1574
00:57:48,967 --> 00:57:50,168
- I cannot comprehend
the civilization

1575
00:57:50,202 --> 00:57:52,037
where intelligent
men like yourselves

1576
00:57:52,070 --> 00:57:55,273
are not permitted to guide
the destinies of their people.

1577
00:57:55,307 --> 00:57:56,440
Very well then.

1578
00:57:56,473 --> 00:57:59,377
You agree to describe
our technology.

1579
00:57:59,410 --> 00:58:01,645
And you will do it so well
that even your government heads

1580
00:58:01,678 --> 00:58:04,548
will realize the
hopelessness of opposing me.

1581
00:58:04,582 --> 00:58:05,917
- [Servo] Alrighty then.

1582
00:58:05,950 --> 00:58:06,952
- You'll make the
necessary arrangements then

1583
00:58:06,985 --> 00:58:08,218
to send us back to Earth?

1584
00:58:08,252 --> 00:58:10,020
- [Phantom] No need of that.

1585
00:58:10,053 --> 00:58:12,457
You can broadcast your
message directly from here.

1586
00:58:12,490 --> 00:58:14,692
- That means that we--
- That's right!

1587
00:58:14,725 --> 00:58:17,928
You may expect to remain
with us for some time.

1588
00:58:17,962 --> 00:58:20,832
Until you have assisted
me with all my plans.

1589
00:58:20,865 --> 00:58:23,602
- [Crow] Bryce, when will
I see you again, Bryce?

1590
00:58:23,635 --> 00:58:26,403
(sinister music)

1591
00:58:27,705 --> 00:58:30,808
- [Mike] I'm gonna
mess you up, boom!

1592
00:58:33,277 --> 00:58:35,880
- [Servo] Beautiful,
just beautiful.

1593
00:58:35,913 --> 00:58:40,050
(suspenseful music)
Like a brainy green of Japan.

1594
00:58:41,385 --> 00:58:43,955
Is this just a really
slow chase scene?

1595
00:58:43,988 --> 00:58:45,055
With one car?

1596
00:58:49,293 --> 00:58:52,963
- [Crow] What, are we driving
through plutonium or--

1597
00:58:52,997 --> 00:58:54,632
- [Mike] It's Garbo.

1598
00:58:54,665 --> 00:58:55,833
- Hey! Wake up!

1599
00:58:57,935 --> 00:58:59,137
Be careful.

1600
00:58:59,170 --> 00:59:00,405
I don't think the
Chief would like it

1601
00:59:00,438 --> 00:59:02,973
if he knew you were
sleeping on the job!

1602
00:59:04,675 --> 00:59:08,345
- [Mike] Hey, wake up,
your egg is hatching.

1603
00:59:08,378 --> 00:59:09,513
- What is it?

1604
00:59:09,547 --> 00:59:10,948
- That's better.

1605
00:59:10,982 --> 00:59:13,050
You heard anything
from the flagship?

1606
00:59:13,083 --> 00:59:14,318
From the Chief?

1607
00:59:14,352 --> 00:59:15,920
- Not since they passed
through the meteor zone.

1608
00:59:15,953 --> 00:59:17,255
- Alright, stay awake!

1609
00:59:17,288 --> 00:59:18,790
- [Crow] Yeah, blow
it out your gizzard.

1610
00:59:18,823 --> 00:59:20,358
- Nothing new.

1611
00:59:20,392 --> 00:59:22,460
We'd better get some kind
of a lead on that Prince

1612
00:59:22,493 --> 00:59:24,762
before the Chief gets here.

1613
00:59:24,795 --> 00:59:27,132
- Sure is funny how he
disappeared without a trace.

1614
00:59:27,165 --> 00:59:30,033
His car, too.
- Get outta the way!

1615
00:59:30,067 --> 00:59:32,570
- I know, but they
don't know anything!

1616
00:59:32,603 --> 00:59:33,872
- The Commissioner
told me they figure

1617
00:59:33,905 --> 00:59:35,840
it must have been the space men.

1618
00:59:35,873 --> 00:59:36,873
- I guess so.

1619
00:59:36,907 --> 00:59:39,210
- It's the only explanation.

1620
00:59:41,612 --> 00:59:42,780
- [Crow] My Slurpee spilled!

1621
00:59:42,813 --> 00:59:44,582
- Pick up something?

1622
00:59:44,615 --> 00:59:48,485
(Tom hums Pop Goes the Weasel)

1623
00:59:49,953 --> 00:59:51,922
- Okay, right foot.

1624
00:59:51,957 --> 00:59:54,392
- [Man With Newspaper]
Don't work so fast.

1625
00:59:54,425 --> 00:59:57,128
(suspenseful music)

1626
00:59:57,162 --> 00:59:59,097
- [Crow] Are you ever
gonna stop farting?

1627
00:59:59,130 --> 01:00:01,967
Is that even a
remote possibility?

1628
01:00:03,233 --> 01:00:04,135
- That's close enough.

1629
01:00:04,168 --> 01:00:07,238
Cut in the automatic search.

1630
01:00:07,272 --> 01:00:09,073
(Tom hums Pop Goes the Weasel)

1631
01:00:09,107 --> 01:00:13,277
- [Servo] Well, no more guns
shelled again last night.

1632
01:00:13,978 --> 01:00:17,048
(suspenseful music)

1633
01:00:17,115 --> 01:00:21,252
Get back to work or you're
back out on the street!

1634
01:00:22,120 --> 01:00:23,788
- It's the shoeshine boy.

1635
01:00:23,822 --> 01:00:24,855
- Put it on the beam.

1636
01:00:24,888 --> 01:00:26,357
- Right.

1637
01:00:26,390 --> 01:00:29,293
(loud buzzing)

1638
01:00:29,327 --> 01:00:32,997
Attention, X-radar get
very high reading of 98

1639
01:00:33,030 --> 01:00:34,465
on shoeshine boy.

1640
01:00:35,500 --> 01:00:36,767
- [Phantom] Tune it in properly!

1641
01:00:36,800 --> 01:00:39,403
- [Mike] Just wiggle it around!

1642
01:00:42,473 --> 01:00:44,442
- [Servo] Check, please.

1643
01:00:44,475 --> 01:00:47,745
(sirens wailing)
Would you mind

1644
01:00:47,778 --> 01:00:49,813
if I paid you in TicTacs?

1645
01:00:53,885 --> 01:00:56,487
- (chuckles) So our Prince
of Space is disguised

1646
01:00:56,520 --> 01:00:58,355
as a miserable bootblack.

1647
01:00:58,388 --> 01:00:59,857
Clever.

1648
01:00:59,890 --> 01:01:02,393
We never would have picked
him up without the X-radar.

1649
01:01:02,427 --> 01:01:03,962
Attention, Earth Patrol.

1650
01:01:03,995 --> 01:01:06,397
This is your Commander
speaking personally to you.

1651
01:01:06,430 --> 01:01:08,733
Now that you have found
this Prince of Space,

1652
01:01:08,767 --> 01:01:11,568
be careful and keep him
in sight at all times.

1653
01:01:11,602 --> 01:01:13,037
- [Crow] Careful!

1654
01:01:13,070 --> 01:01:14,872
He'll try to sell you
shoelaces with your shine!

1655
01:01:14,905 --> 01:01:16,473
- You heard what he said.

1656
01:01:16,507 --> 01:01:18,508
- [Servo] Yeah, whatever.

1657
01:01:18,542 --> 01:01:19,677
- [Mike] Can I
just learn to read

1658
01:01:19,710 --> 01:01:22,380
and then I'll come back to work?

1659
01:01:23,680 --> 01:01:25,650
- [Crow] I got a bootblack
down at the track,

1660
01:01:25,683 --> 01:01:29,187
yup, big bootblacking
thing goin' on.

1661
01:01:29,220 --> 01:01:30,822
- [Servo] Hey, bootblack,
congratulations!

1662
01:01:30,855 --> 01:01:32,923
What did you do?

1663
01:01:32,957 --> 01:01:34,292
- Mr. Tannen!

1664
01:01:34,325 --> 01:01:35,993
Hey, Mr. Tannen!

1665
01:01:36,027 --> 01:01:38,730
- Get out of my wine!
- You forgot this.

1666
01:01:38,763 --> 01:01:40,565
You're getting absentminded.

1667
01:01:40,598 --> 01:01:42,200
- [Crow] Be healed!

1668
01:01:43,768 --> 01:01:47,938
(chuckles) Man, I
hate that bastard.

1669
01:01:51,275 --> 01:01:53,210
- [Mike] You carry
Bootblack Journal?

1670
01:01:53,243 --> 01:01:54,078
No?

1671
01:01:55,078 --> 01:01:56,313
- [Crow] Ah, here it is!

1672
01:01:56,313 --> 01:02:00,017
Little Baby Sunhats
Monthly! (chuckles)

1673
01:02:00,852 --> 01:02:01,585
- Scalpel.
- What happened?

1674
01:02:01,618 --> 01:02:02,787
- He ran away.

1675
01:02:03,755 --> 01:02:05,055
- He came back.

1676
01:02:05,088 --> 01:02:06,790
It's alright now.
- No, wait.

1677
01:02:06,823 --> 01:02:08,125
He ran away again.

1678
01:02:08,158 --> 01:02:11,895
- [Phantom] Attention,
Earth Patrol, attention.

1679
01:02:11,928 --> 01:02:14,965
We will arrive over
the city in 30 seconds.

1680
01:02:14,998 --> 01:02:17,668
- [Crow] We better
clean this place up!

1681
01:02:17,702 --> 01:02:20,872
- Report any suspicious
movements when we
appear in the sky.

1682
01:02:20,905 --> 01:02:25,075
- [Servo] I had a suspicious
moment after breakfast!

1683
01:02:26,510 --> 01:02:29,080
- [Henchman] Full
descent to 500 feet.

1684
01:02:29,113 --> 01:02:30,782
- [Crow] Set whole
friers to stun!

1685
01:02:30,848 --> 01:02:33,150
(loud zing)

1686
01:02:34,518 --> 01:02:37,155
- [Servo] The upper half
of a Hopper painting.

1687
01:02:37,188 --> 01:02:39,523
(people shout)
Oh! A giant roast chicken!

1688
01:02:39,557 --> 01:02:40,458
- [Crow] It is brown
on the outside,

1689
01:02:40,492 --> 01:02:41,925
tender and juicy on the inside!

1690
01:02:41,958 --> 01:02:45,295
- [Mike] It is not fermented
pickle or raw, wrong!

1691
01:02:45,328 --> 01:02:47,698
- [Crow] Potatoes are stuffing!

1692
01:02:47,732 --> 01:02:50,768
(people shout)

1693
01:02:50,802 --> 01:02:54,972
♪ When I was Japanese,
it was a very good year ♪

1694
01:02:56,407 --> 01:02:57,608
- [Crow] Oh!

1695
01:02:57,642 --> 01:02:58,442
Ice dams!

1696
01:02:58,475 --> 01:02:59,910
We have ice dams!

1697
01:03:01,345 --> 01:03:02,713
- [Servo] It may not be relevant

1698
01:03:02,747 --> 01:03:04,515
but did you know that
Gamera's friend to children?

1699
01:03:04,548 --> 01:03:06,417
- [Mike] Gamera, oh, he's
made of turtle meat, right?

1700
01:03:06,450 --> 01:03:08,052
- [Servo] Yes, really neat.

1701
01:03:08,085 --> 01:03:12,257
(loud zing)
(people shout)

1702
01:03:13,390 --> 01:03:15,693
- [Crow] I like that very much!

1703
01:03:15,727 --> 01:03:18,830
("MST3K Love Theme")

1704
01:03:22,733 --> 01:03:24,902
Sir, they called us weenies.
- Sir, we are ready

1705
01:03:24,935 --> 01:03:28,105
with the all-wave transmitter.

1706
01:03:28,138 --> 01:03:31,942
- [Servo] Ah, sir, you
left an egg on the chair.

1707
01:03:31,975 --> 01:03:33,577
- Give me the microphone.

1708
01:03:33,610 --> 01:03:35,078
Put Professor Macken
on the screen.

1709
01:03:35,112 --> 01:03:37,080
- [Servo] The camera loves him.

1710
01:03:37,080 --> 01:03:38,482
- Attention.

1711
01:03:38,515 --> 01:03:41,485
People of Earth, I have an
important announcement to make!

1712
01:03:41,518 --> 01:03:44,588
One that you've been
waiting for a long time.

1713
01:03:44,622 --> 01:03:48,792
Up here with me, I have the
famous Professor Macken!

1714
01:03:50,227 --> 01:03:53,230
A name you all recognize who
has agreed to speak to you

1715
01:03:53,263 --> 01:03:55,065
on my behalf.

1716
01:03:55,098 --> 01:03:56,400
Go ahead, Professor.

1717
01:03:56,433 --> 01:03:58,335
- [Servo] Hey, the
Japanese Sylvia Plath.

1718
01:03:58,368 --> 01:03:59,903
- [Professor] For
the past 24 hours,

1719
01:03:59,937 --> 01:04:02,740
I and several of my
colleagues have been captives

1720
01:04:02,773 --> 01:04:06,143
aboard the flagship of
the person who just spoke.

1721
01:04:06,177 --> 01:04:08,545
The dictator of Krankor.

1722
01:04:08,578 --> 01:04:10,280
For most of that time,
(Mike and robots chuckle)

1723
01:04:10,347 --> 01:04:13,483
we have been captive
witnesses of a state

1724
01:04:13,517 --> 01:04:17,120
of military technology
capable of destroying any

1725
01:04:17,153 --> 01:04:20,223
of the great metropolitan
centers of Earth.

1726
01:04:20,257 --> 01:04:22,260
In order to
demonstrate his power,

1727
01:04:22,293 --> 01:04:24,728
the dictator intends to
wipe out one of our cities

1728
01:04:24,762 --> 01:04:26,463
at noon tomorrow.

1729
01:04:26,497 --> 01:04:29,833
The only way to prevent
this is for all nations

1730
01:04:29,867 --> 01:04:31,768
and all the governments
of this planet

1731
01:04:31,802 --> 01:04:35,238
to agree to accept his terms
for unconditional surrender!

1732
01:04:35,272 --> 01:04:36,673
People of Earth, listen to me!

1733
01:04:36,707 --> 01:04:38,675
You've only one
response to make!

1734
01:04:38,708 --> 01:04:41,112
Bomb the (mumbles)!
- Bomb the ayrower?

1735
01:04:41,145 --> 01:04:43,247
- Very good.
- Ayrower!

1736
01:04:43,313 --> 01:04:44,448
- Put him back in his quarters.

1737
01:04:44,482 --> 01:04:45,650
- [Mike] Get him some ties.

1738
01:04:45,683 --> 01:04:47,452
- Put me on the screen.

1739
01:04:47,485 --> 01:04:49,453
- Come on, this way.

1740
01:04:49,487 --> 01:04:51,722
Get going.
(suspenseful music)

1741
01:04:51,755 --> 01:04:52,923
- Alright.

1742
01:04:52,957 --> 01:04:55,525
As you can see, your
Professor is indisposed.

1743
01:04:55,558 --> 01:04:56,693
So I'll address

1744
01:04:56,727 --> 01:04:57,895
you personally.
- Daddy, this is fun!

1745
01:04:57,928 --> 01:04:58,762
Go faster!

1746
01:04:59,897 --> 01:05:03,633
Raise your hands if
you'd like to go faster!

1747
01:05:03,667 --> 01:05:05,502
- [Phantom] And as Professor
Macken has told you,

1748
01:05:05,535 --> 01:05:07,672
if I so wished, I could
at this very moment

1749
01:05:07,705 --> 01:05:10,240
wipe your entire
city off the map.

1750
01:05:10,273 --> 01:05:11,542
- Turn to Full House!
- I can do the same

1751
01:05:11,575 --> 01:05:14,812
to New York, Paris,
Rome, Berlin, Moscow!

1752
01:05:14,845 --> 01:05:17,648
All of your great
metropolitan centers!

1753
01:05:17,682 --> 01:05:19,550
There's nothing to stop me!

1754
01:05:19,583 --> 01:05:21,118
For I have completely paralyzed

1755
01:05:21,152 --> 01:05:23,320
all of your primitive
defense measures!

1756
01:05:23,353 --> 01:05:25,222
Your radar cannot find me,

1757
01:05:25,255 --> 01:05:27,658
your fastest jet planes
would be destroyed

1758
01:05:27,692 --> 01:05:29,527
the moment they approach
my headquarters.

1759
01:05:29,560 --> 01:05:30,728
- The hell is this?
- So you are wise

1760
01:05:30,762 --> 01:05:32,162
to keep your war planes grounded

1761
01:05:32,195 --> 01:05:35,165
and listen to me
quietly and calmly.

1762
01:05:35,198 --> 01:05:38,168
I have come to offer you
a choice between peace

1763
01:05:38,202 --> 01:05:40,237
or extermination.

1764
01:05:40,270 --> 01:05:43,373
If you do not accept my demand
for unconditional surrender,

1765
01:05:43,373 --> 01:05:45,375
I will destroy you.

1766
01:05:45,408 --> 01:05:48,045
But if you accept me
willingly as your ruler,

1767
01:05:48,078 --> 01:05:50,613
your entire planet will
enter upon a period of peace

1768
01:05:50,613 --> 01:05:52,650
and prosperity such
as it has never known

1769
01:05:52,683 --> 01:05:54,385
in all its recorded history.

1770
01:05:54,418 --> 01:05:55,653
- [Servo] Okay, we give in!

1771
01:05:55,687 --> 01:05:57,053
- [Phantom] You have 24 hours

1772
01:05:57,087 --> 01:05:59,557
to make your wishes known to me.

1773
01:05:59,590 --> 01:06:01,858
I will return tomorrow.

1774
01:06:01,892 --> 01:06:03,693
You will tell me then
whether you prefer

1775
01:06:03,727 --> 01:06:06,897
(Crow hums)
to surrender or die.

1776
01:06:06,930 --> 01:06:09,867
(laughs evilly)
(Tom gasps)

1777
01:06:09,900 --> 01:06:13,170
- [Crow] Oh, and we need worms!

1778
01:06:13,203 --> 01:06:15,472
(loud zing)
(people scream)

1779
01:06:15,505 --> 01:06:19,010
- [Mike] It's going
to rain giblets on us!

1780
01:06:19,043 --> 01:06:21,945
- [Servo] The Prince
of Indecision!

1781
01:06:23,713 --> 01:06:27,885
- Wally, come on, let's get
out of here, Wally, come on.

1782
01:06:29,053 --> 01:06:31,188
- [Crow] Well, back
into the fart mobile.

1783
01:06:31,222 --> 01:06:34,225
I still like
bootblacking very much!

1784
01:06:35,192 --> 01:06:38,195
(Tom clucks softly)

1785
01:06:39,263 --> 01:06:41,898
Come on, slave
labor, I mean kids!

1786
01:06:45,870 --> 01:06:48,472
- Chief, Prince is walking away.

1787
01:06:48,505 --> 01:06:49,940
We'll follow him.

1788
01:06:49,973 --> 01:06:51,475
Go on, follow him.

1789
01:06:51,508 --> 01:06:52,677
- [Phantom] Stay with him.

1790
01:06:52,710 --> 01:06:54,278
Don't let him out of your sight!

1791
01:06:54,312 --> 01:06:56,447
But above all, don't let
him know you are following!

1792
01:06:56,480 --> 01:06:58,315
I will be there tonight
and I want to be able

1793
01:06:58,348 --> 01:07:00,317
to take him at once!
(soft clucking)

1794
01:07:00,350 --> 01:07:01,585
- [Mike] You ever
get the feeling

1795
01:07:01,618 --> 01:07:04,455
Krankor is just wingin' it?
- Oh, yeah.

1796
01:07:06,090 --> 01:07:06,990
- [Servo] We'll go to a land

1797
01:07:07,023 --> 01:07:09,493
where we are free to bootblack!

1798
01:07:09,527 --> 01:07:12,530
(suspenseful music)

1799
01:07:14,298 --> 01:07:15,900
Buuuck, buuuuuck...

1800
01:07:17,702 --> 01:07:18,902
My egg is crowning!

1801
01:07:18,935 --> 01:07:20,470
- I wonder how far
he's going to walk.

1802
01:07:20,503 --> 01:07:22,573
- Until we stop following him.

1803
01:07:22,607 --> 01:07:24,742
- Never mind the jokes.
- Sorry for my zaniness.

1804
01:07:24,775 --> 01:07:27,377
- They're going into the house.

1805
01:07:28,778 --> 01:07:31,515
(suspenseful music)
- I am going to bootblack

1806
01:07:31,548 --> 01:07:32,450
in my room.

1807
01:07:36,853 --> 01:07:40,858
- [Crow] Kimmy, don't eat
all the jellied squid!

1808
01:07:41,892 --> 01:07:43,893
- [Mike] Cram it, world.

1809
01:07:49,600 --> 01:07:51,702
- Ah, home at last.

1810
01:07:51,735 --> 01:07:53,737
Good boy, Mickey, gonna
feed the bird, huh?

1811
01:07:53,770 --> 01:07:55,272
- What difference does it make?

1812
01:07:55,305 --> 01:07:57,742
That mean dictator's gonna
burn us all up anyhow.

1813
01:07:57,775 --> 01:07:59,008
- I want the Prince of Space.

1814
01:07:59,042 --> 01:08:00,477
He's the only one
who could help us.

1815
01:08:00,510 --> 01:08:02,780
- Don't worry, Mickey,
he'll surely help us out.

1816
01:08:02,847 --> 01:08:05,148
- You think so?
- Course he will!

1817
01:08:05,182 --> 01:08:07,383
He always came before, right?

1818
01:08:07,417 --> 01:08:08,852
Didn't he, Mickey?

1819
01:08:08,885 --> 01:08:11,255
- Oh, I think he's gone
away and forgotten about us.

1820
01:08:11,288 --> 01:08:12,890
- [Servo] The bird left
a letter of resignation.

1821
01:08:12,923 --> 01:08:14,458
- Hey!

1822
01:08:14,492 --> 01:08:16,060
- [Mike] Leave 50 cuttle
bones under the bridge

1823
01:08:16,093 --> 01:08:17,628
or I start spotting your car.

1824
01:08:17,662 --> 01:08:18,962
- It's for me.

1825
01:08:18,995 --> 01:08:20,630
Dear Mickey, go
to Johnny's house

1826
01:08:20,663 --> 01:08:22,398
right away with your sister.

1827
01:08:22,432 --> 01:08:24,835
Signed, Prince of Space.

1828
01:08:24,868 --> 01:08:26,870
Hey, Wally, what do
you think about that?

1829
01:08:26,903 --> 01:08:28,772
- [Kimmy] Listen to what
the note said, Mickey!

1830
01:08:28,805 --> 01:08:30,073
- No, wait a minute.

1831
01:08:30,107 --> 01:08:32,408
Who could put a note
like this up in a cage?

1832
01:08:32,442 --> 01:08:34,043
- Never mind that,
get a move on!

1833
01:08:34,077 --> 01:08:35,913
You wanna do what
the note says, right?

1834
01:08:35,947 --> 01:08:38,048
- Right, yeah,
come on, let's go.

1835
01:08:38,082 --> 01:08:39,283
- [Kimmy] Alright,
goodbye, Wally.

1836
01:08:39,317 --> 01:08:40,985
Don't worry about us,
go one with your dinner.

1837
01:08:41,018 --> 01:08:42,252
- [Mickey] Hurry,
Kimmy, come on.

1838
01:08:42,285 --> 01:08:46,190
- I'm coming, you hurry!
- I love that kid!

1839
01:08:46,223 --> 01:08:49,627
Finally, an evening
alone together.

1840
01:08:49,660 --> 01:08:52,597
(Mike and robots gasp)
- We got chickens!

1841
01:08:52,630 --> 01:08:54,265
(thrilling music)

1842
01:08:54,298 --> 01:08:58,002
- [Servo] I don't wanna
be Prince of Space!

1843
01:08:58,035 --> 01:08:59,237
- [Crow] Wait,
where are you going?

1844
01:08:59,270 --> 01:09:01,205
Come back and let
us capture you!

1845
01:09:01,238 --> 01:09:05,408
(Mike and robots
cluck repeatedly)

1846
01:09:08,112 --> 01:09:09,280
- [Servo] Exotic locations

1847
01:09:09,313 --> 01:09:11,515
like Normandale
Community College!

1848
01:09:11,548 --> 01:09:12,750
- The Chief is on
his way to meet us!

1849
01:09:12,783 --> 01:09:13,983
What are we gonna do?

1850
01:09:14,017 --> 01:09:16,887
- Just keep the
radio beam going.

1851
01:09:16,920 --> 01:09:19,223
- [Servo] That's some
hauling ass, whew!

1852
01:09:19,257 --> 01:09:20,823
- Halt, or we fire!

1853
01:09:22,827 --> 01:09:24,662
- [Crow] Well, his sight's
are pullin' about 60 yards

1854
01:09:24,695 --> 01:09:27,532
to the left there. (chuckles)

1855
01:09:27,565 --> 01:09:31,735
(Mike and robots cluck loudly)

1856
01:09:32,870 --> 01:09:36,473
- [Servo] I brought
grub worms for everyone!

1857
01:09:37,207 --> 01:09:38,675
- After 'em that way!

1858
01:09:38,708 --> 01:09:41,012
- [Mike] Deploy your tiny
whippers only if necessary!

1859
01:09:41,045 --> 01:09:44,682
(eerie twang)
(thrilling music)

1860
01:09:44,715 --> 01:09:45,983
- [Servo] Maybe they
just came to this planet

1861
01:09:46,017 --> 01:09:47,652
to serve the guy a subpoena.

1862
01:09:47,685 --> 01:09:50,220
(loud explosion)
Look at them.

1863
01:09:50,253 --> 01:09:53,057
(thrilling music)

1864
01:09:54,825 --> 01:09:58,728
Even in death they're
stacked on top of each other.

1865
01:09:58,762 --> 01:10:00,763
(Mike and robots cluck loudly)

1866
01:10:00,797 --> 01:10:03,567
(loud explosion)

1867
01:10:06,103 --> 01:10:07,170
- Ah!

1868
01:10:07,203 --> 01:10:08,405
Prince of Space!

1869
01:10:08,438 --> 01:10:09,907
- [Servo] I was
thinking it was going

1870
01:10:09,940 --> 01:10:11,808
to be Fritz Mondale, but of
course, it's Prince of Space!

1871
01:10:11,842 --> 01:10:14,043
(loud explosions)

1872
01:10:14,077 --> 01:10:17,413
- Hold your fire!
- You guys look ridiculous!

1873
01:10:17,413 --> 01:10:18,848
- Your weapons are useless!

1874
01:10:18,882 --> 01:10:21,418
Let's try bare hands now!

1875
01:10:21,452 --> 01:10:23,687
- [Mike] Up at 'em,
Prince of Space!

1876
01:10:23,720 --> 01:10:24,888
- [Crow] His power
apparently lies

1877
01:10:24,922 --> 01:10:27,925
in his choosing
incompetent enemies.

1878
01:10:30,060 --> 01:10:33,763
- [Servo] The merchants
are here, we're saved!

1879
01:10:33,797 --> 01:10:35,665
They're on to you, I gotta go!

1880
01:10:35,698 --> 01:10:39,102
(thrilling music)

1881
01:10:39,135 --> 01:10:39,970
The hell?

1882
01:10:41,638 --> 01:10:44,775
- [Crow] Oh, hi, cherry, huh?

1883
01:10:44,808 --> 01:10:45,977
- You again!

1884
01:10:46,010 --> 01:10:47,945
- [Phantom] Yes, it's me!

1885
01:10:47,978 --> 01:10:50,047
I've come to finish you off!

1886
01:10:50,047 --> 01:10:51,548
- [Crow] What a vicious cycle.

1887
01:10:51,582 --> 01:10:53,917
(ray guns zing loudly)

1888
01:10:53,950 --> 01:10:55,585
- [Servo] I figure
he'll get bored and die

1889
01:10:55,618 --> 01:10:59,790
and then I will rule! (chuckles)

1890
01:11:01,125 --> 01:11:03,893
- [Mike] Now even I'm
beginning to doubt my powers.

1891
01:11:03,927 --> 01:11:06,563
- (laughs) You see?

1892
01:11:06,597 --> 01:11:08,732
How many times do I have
to demonstrate to you?

1893
01:11:08,765 --> 01:11:10,367
Your guns are
worthless against me!

1894
01:11:10,400 --> 01:11:12,468
- Argh, come closer!

1895
01:11:12,502 --> 01:11:14,472
- I'm close enough,
thank you anyway!

1896
01:11:14,505 --> 01:11:15,705
The stench of your foul breath

1897
01:11:15,738 --> 01:11:17,307
is more than my
stomach can stand!

1898
01:11:17,340 --> 01:11:18,142
- Chief, let's go!

1899
01:11:18,175 --> 01:11:18,975
- Get away.

1900
01:11:19,008 --> 01:11:20,543
Fire, fire!

1901
01:11:20,577 --> 01:11:22,512
(thrilling music)
(ray guns fire repeatedly)

1902
01:11:22,545 --> 01:11:26,450
- [Crow] Sorry, sir,
you do have bad breath.

1903
01:11:26,483 --> 01:11:28,018
- [Servo] I feel good all under!

1904
01:11:28,052 --> 01:11:30,853
(ray gun fires repeatedly)

1905
01:11:30,887 --> 01:11:32,723
Oh boy, hey wait
up, I need a ride!

1906
01:11:32,757 --> 01:11:36,593
I didn't mean that about
your breath, come on!

1907
01:11:40,097 --> 01:11:42,833
- [Henchman] Chief, in the stern
window, that flying saucer!

1908
01:11:42,867 --> 01:11:45,702
- [Servo] It's Meer, limping
into a service station.

1909
01:11:45,735 --> 01:11:47,337
- What do we do?
- Get them out of here!

1910
01:11:47,370 --> 01:11:48,472
Put them in their quarters!

1911
01:11:48,505 --> 01:11:49,773
- Do it!
- Alright!

1912
01:11:49,807 --> 01:11:51,075
Back to your rooms!

1913
01:11:51,108 --> 01:11:52,777
- [Crow] Chickens are
too stupid to mutiny.

1914
01:11:52,810 --> 01:11:55,645
(thrilling music)

1915
01:11:57,513 --> 01:12:01,118
- [Servo] My chest (mumbles)
soap dish will help me.

1916
01:12:01,152 --> 01:12:03,253
- [Henchman] What are
we going to do, Chief?

1917
01:12:03,287 --> 01:12:04,755
- Let him come.

1918
01:12:04,788 --> 01:12:06,457
We'll never survive another
trip through the meteor zone.

1919
01:12:06,490 --> 01:12:09,527
But just to make sure,
prepare the costing vapor!

1920
01:12:09,560 --> 01:12:12,062
(doors close)

1921
01:12:21,705 --> 01:12:23,940
(birds chirping)

1922
01:12:23,973 --> 01:12:25,408
- Well, this is good, huh, okay.

1923
01:12:25,442 --> 01:12:26,943
Everything seems to
be back to normal.

1924
01:12:26,977 --> 01:12:30,547
I'm a befleshed human being
(chuckles) and you guys are--

1925
01:12:30,580 --> 01:12:31,415
Oh no.

1926
01:12:32,448 --> 01:12:33,283
Oh no!

1927
01:12:35,218 --> 01:12:36,587
- Uh, Mike?

1928
01:12:36,620 --> 01:12:38,922
Why are we in a sylvan glen?

1929
01:12:38,955 --> 01:12:41,725
- (sneezes loudly)
Hey, I got hay fever!

1930
01:12:41,758 --> 01:12:43,027
Cool! (laughs)

1931
01:12:43,060 --> 01:12:44,628
- I'm gonna--

1932
01:12:44,662 --> 01:12:46,997
I'm gonna go lay down
till this all blows over.

1933
01:12:47,030 --> 01:12:48,565
I'll see you later.

1934
01:12:48,598 --> 01:12:50,667
- I may need a Kleenex!

1935
01:12:50,700 --> 01:12:52,002
- You're fine.

1936
01:12:52,035 --> 01:12:55,838
(Tom sniffs)
- Poor guy.

1937
01:12:55,872 --> 01:12:59,142
He doesn't handle alternate
realities very well, does he?

1938
01:12:59,175 --> 01:13:02,412
- (sneezes loudly) Sorry.

1939
01:13:02,412 --> 01:13:03,213
(sighs)

1940
01:13:03,213 --> 01:13:04,113
- Huh.
- Hm.

1941
01:13:05,115 --> 01:13:07,217
- Still, nice day, though.

1942
01:13:07,250 --> 01:13:08,818
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

1943
01:13:10,453 --> 01:13:13,890
(birds chirping)
Fishin'?

1944
01:13:15,158 --> 01:13:16,827
- No, thanks.
- Okay.

1945
01:13:18,562 --> 01:13:21,665
("MST3K Love Theme")

1946
01:13:24,902 --> 01:13:26,068
(Tom groans)
- You okay?

1947
01:13:26,103 --> 01:13:27,503
- Yeah, oh God.
- He's heading

1948
01:13:27,537 --> 01:13:28,972
right for the center.

1949
01:13:29,005 --> 01:13:31,208
Those meteorites will pound
him to pieces in a few minutes.

1950
01:13:31,242 --> 01:13:33,710
(laughs evilly)

1951
01:13:33,743 --> 01:13:35,745
- [Mike] Yep, I'm the man!

1952
01:13:35,778 --> 01:13:38,548
- Alright, I think we've
seen the last of him!

1953
01:13:38,582 --> 01:13:41,318
He'll never come
out of that alive!

1954
01:13:41,352 --> 01:13:44,455
Give everyone four hours off.
(Mike and robots laugh)

1955
01:13:44,488 --> 01:13:45,755
- [Servo] Sir, did
you forget something

1956
01:13:45,788 --> 01:13:46,990
when you got dressed
this morning?

1957
01:13:47,023 --> 01:13:47,925
- [Mike] Oh, oh, put--

1958
01:13:47,958 --> 01:13:49,493
No.
(Tom laughs)

1959
01:13:49,527 --> 01:13:53,730
(loud zinging)
- Planet International falls.

1960
01:13:56,467 --> 01:13:59,268
(gasps) There he is again!

1961
01:13:59,302 --> 01:14:00,203
- [Mike] Just ignoring the fact

1962
01:14:00,237 --> 01:14:02,338
they have a giant out there?

1963
01:14:02,372 --> 01:14:04,942
- [Servo] The USC losers!

1964
01:14:04,975 --> 01:14:09,112
- Just in case, tell the giant
he better keep awake tonight.

1965
01:14:09,713 --> 01:14:10,913
You never know.

1966
01:14:10,947 --> 01:14:13,483
He might get through
those meteorites.

1967
01:14:13,517 --> 01:14:15,652
Bring those Earthlings
into the great hall.

1968
01:14:15,685 --> 01:14:19,857
- [Crow] Well, time for our
daily empty threat session!

1969
01:14:21,325 --> 01:14:22,525
- [Servo] Krankor will be
with you in a few moments.

1970
01:14:22,558 --> 01:14:24,628
Appointments kind
of backed up today.

1971
01:14:24,662 --> 01:14:26,797
You can have a seat there.

1972
01:14:28,198 --> 01:14:29,198
- Sit down.

1973
01:14:29,232 --> 01:14:30,400
Hey, sit down!

1974
01:14:31,968 --> 01:14:33,170
Sit down, I told you!

1975
01:14:33,203 --> 01:14:34,505
- [Crow] Come on, this
is getting embarrassing!

1976
01:14:34,538 --> 01:14:35,372
- What do I have to do?

1977
01:14:35,405 --> 01:14:36,873
I told you to sit down!

1978
01:14:36,907 --> 01:14:38,742
- [Mike] Oh, you knocked
him slightly off balance.

1979
01:14:38,775 --> 01:14:41,378
- [Servo] Must be reported
to Amnesty International!

1980
01:14:41,412 --> 01:14:43,113
- [Mike] Or the USDA.

1981
01:14:44,782 --> 01:14:47,583
- (chuckles) Maybe
you'll listen to me now.

1982
01:14:47,617 --> 01:14:50,787
- [Crow] Chickens
are a cruel people.

1983
01:14:50,820 --> 01:14:53,990
(suspenseful music)
- (clears throat) Okay,

1984
01:14:54,023 --> 01:14:54,992
who called this meeting?

1985
01:14:55,025 --> 01:14:55,892
- I didn't.
- I didn't!

1986
01:14:55,925 --> 01:14:57,193
- No.
- We don't?

1987
01:15:00,697 --> 01:15:02,198
- [Servo] Lucille?

1988
01:15:04,000 --> 01:15:05,002
Whoa!

1989
01:15:05,035 --> 01:15:07,103
- [Crow] Get the DeSoto started.

1990
01:15:07,137 --> 01:15:08,505
(suspenseful music)

1991
01:15:08,538 --> 01:15:09,740
- Hey, what's that?

1992
01:15:09,773 --> 01:15:11,342
A rocket!

1993
01:15:11,375 --> 01:15:14,377
- [Mike] Oh no, it's
just duct work, okay.

1994
01:15:14,410 --> 01:15:18,548
(loud whirring)
(loud clank)

1995
01:15:20,283 --> 01:15:23,253
- [Servo] Krankor is
Mary, Queen of Scots.

1996
01:15:23,287 --> 01:15:24,453
- [Crow] Taxi!

1997
01:15:27,057 --> 01:15:29,893
- [Mike] Go ahead on three.

1998
01:15:29,927 --> 01:15:32,628
(Tom gasps in amazement)

1999
01:15:32,662 --> 01:15:33,997
- [Crow] Oh, please not this.

2000
01:15:34,030 --> 01:15:36,867
Anything but an
old Star Trek set!

2001
01:15:39,402 --> 01:15:42,105
- Here, you see Krankor.

2002
01:15:42,138 --> 01:15:46,042
A part of my domain which
no man has ever seen.

2003
01:15:46,075 --> 01:15:49,278
It is the last thing which
you will see in this life.

2004
01:15:49,278 --> 01:15:51,248
- [Mike] So, how are you guys?

2005
01:15:51,282 --> 01:15:52,682
- [Doctor] What do you mean?

2006
01:15:52,715 --> 01:15:53,917
- [Professor] What
do you mean by that?

2007
01:15:53,950 --> 01:15:54,752
- Look!

2008
01:15:56,387 --> 01:15:57,487
What's that?

2009
01:15:57,520 --> 01:16:00,357
- [Servo] (gasps) Cecil Fielder!

2010
01:16:00,390 --> 01:16:01,725
- Do you see that?

2011
01:16:01,758 --> 01:16:03,293
What the devil is that?

2012
01:16:03,327 --> 01:16:04,795
- It's the monster
which guards this place.

2013
01:16:04,828 --> 01:16:05,628
- You hear that?

2014
01:16:05,662 --> 01:16:07,197
A monster!

2015
01:16:07,230 --> 01:16:08,998
- Quite right, my dear Macken.

2016
01:16:09,032 --> 01:16:11,067
A monster which I created.

2017
01:16:11,100 --> 01:16:12,835
He obeys my slightest command.

2018
01:16:12,868 --> 01:16:15,638
- [Crow] Like wander around
aimlessly and gain weight!

2019
01:16:15,672 --> 01:16:17,807
(Mike and Tom chuckle)

2020
01:16:17,840 --> 01:16:19,777
- [Henchman] The guardian
has moved into position.

2021
01:16:19,810 --> 01:16:22,645
All persons are warned
to stay clear of him.

2022
01:16:22,678 --> 01:16:24,815
- Very good.
- Give yourself a star.

2023
01:16:24,848 --> 01:16:26,783
- Now, gentlemen,
your time has come.

2024
01:16:26,817 --> 01:16:28,752
Prepare to leave Krankor.

2025
01:16:28,785 --> 01:16:31,988
- What's that?
- Prepare to leave.

2026
01:16:32,022 --> 01:16:35,492
Each of you will
enter a space capsule.

2027
01:16:35,525 --> 01:16:36,660
- What?

2028
01:16:36,693 --> 01:16:38,428
(Mike laughs)
- Each of you

2029
01:16:38,462 --> 01:16:40,697
will enter a space capsule!

2030
01:16:41,932 --> 01:16:43,133
- [Phantom] It'll be sealed up.

2031
01:16:43,133 --> 01:16:45,235
Each one of you in turn
will then blast off

2032
01:16:45,268 --> 01:16:47,737
and travel far, far out
in the furthest reaches

2033
01:16:47,770 --> 01:16:49,238
of the galaxy.
- Come again?

2034
01:16:49,272 --> 01:16:51,173
- [Phantom] Your course
will be selected at random

2035
01:16:51,207 --> 01:16:52,675
and will ultimately
be determined

2036
01:16:52,708 --> 01:16:55,212
by the celestial bodies
near which you pass.

2037
01:16:55,245 --> 01:16:56,413
- What'd he say?
- Those of you

2038
01:16:56,413 --> 01:16:58,848
who are fortunate
will fall into a star.

2039
01:16:58,882 --> 01:17:00,717
- How's that?
- The agony will be horrible,

2040
01:17:00,750 --> 01:17:02,585
but it will be brief.
- Beg pardon?

2041
01:17:02,618 --> 01:17:03,820
- [Phantom] The first
rocket will be manned

2042
01:17:03,853 --> 01:17:04,955
by Dr. Macken.
- You know,

2043
01:17:04,988 --> 01:17:06,088
wouldn't it cheaper and quicker

2044
01:17:06,122 --> 01:17:08,792
to just bludgeon 'em right here?

2045
01:17:10,493 --> 01:17:13,730
(Mike grunts)

2046
01:17:13,763 --> 01:17:15,432
- [Phantom] Why, Dr.
Macken, you surprise me!

2047
01:17:15,465 --> 01:17:17,333
- [Servo] I thought
you were a total puss!

2048
01:17:17,367 --> 01:17:18,835
- You look so glum.

2049
01:17:18,868 --> 01:17:22,538
After all, you preferred not
to surrender. (laughs evilly)

2050
01:17:23,673 --> 01:17:27,210
- [Crow] Hey, don't
moon me over there, hey!

2051
01:17:27,243 --> 01:17:30,580
- [Mike] Yup, agonizing
death, no doubt about it.

2052
01:17:30,580 --> 01:17:31,415
Yeah.

2053
01:17:33,450 --> 01:17:35,685
- [Servo] Sir, we only have
two ships, can we double up?

2054
01:17:35,718 --> 01:17:36,853
- What?

2055
01:17:36,887 --> 01:17:38,088
The Prince of Space?

2056
01:17:38,122 --> 01:17:39,088
- He's coming!

2057
01:17:39,122 --> 01:17:40,323
Prince of Space!

2058
01:17:40,357 --> 01:17:41,525
Prince of Space!

2059
01:17:41,558 --> 01:17:42,758
He's coming!

2060
01:17:42,792 --> 01:17:43,993
- [Servo] Tickets at all
Ticketmaster outlets.

2061
01:17:44,027 --> 01:17:44,828
- Oh!

2062
01:17:44,862 --> 01:17:46,228
There he is!

2063
01:17:46,262 --> 01:17:49,132
(thrilling music)
- Hi, be right with you--

2064
01:17:49,165 --> 01:17:50,300
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

2065
01:17:50,333 --> 01:17:51,768
- What a fool!
- He has defeated us

2066
01:17:51,802 --> 01:17:54,337
numerous times, what makes
him think he can do it again?

2067
01:17:54,370 --> 01:17:56,440
- The guardian will make
mincemeat out of him!

2068
01:17:56,473 --> 01:17:59,642
He'll smash that miserable
fool once and for all!

2069
01:17:59,675 --> 01:18:02,645
♪ In the land of Dairy Queen ♪

2070
01:18:02,645 --> 01:18:05,215
(loud zinging)

2071
01:18:06,082 --> 01:18:07,150
We're closed!

2072
01:18:11,320 --> 01:18:13,723
He looks like a welderer
who has fainting spells.

2073
01:18:13,757 --> 01:18:16,258
(Mike chuckles)

2074
01:18:16,292 --> 01:18:17,793
- [Crow] Ross Perot!

2075
01:18:17,827 --> 01:18:21,965
- [Servo] This is starting
to become a weird movie.

2076
01:18:21,998 --> 01:18:25,235
Ah, he kills with an
enormous air burp!

2077
01:18:26,770 --> 01:18:30,207
- [Mike] Um, what was
that supposed to do?

2078
01:18:30,240 --> 01:18:33,343
- [Crow] (chuckles)
It's Pat! (chuckles)

2079
01:18:33,377 --> 01:18:34,978
- [Servo] Gonna take a
look at the manual here.

2080
01:18:35,012 --> 01:18:38,915
There's giants, ah, big-eared
matronly giants, page 12.

2081
01:18:38,948 --> 01:18:41,518
(loud zinging)

2082
01:18:43,653 --> 01:18:47,823
- [Crow] Mrs. Robinson, are
you trying to seduce me?

2083
01:18:48,558 --> 01:18:49,592
- [Servo] Bless you!

2084
01:18:50,993 --> 01:18:51,828
Hmm, what?

2085
01:18:54,030 --> 01:18:56,132
- [Mike] Well, not today.

2086
01:18:58,402 --> 01:19:02,538
- [Crow] Some monsters
just should not wear belts.

2087
01:19:07,510 --> 01:19:10,047
- [Mike] Oh, he's a
yam with features!

2088
01:19:10,047 --> 01:19:13,217
(loud zings)

2089
01:19:13,250 --> 01:19:17,187
- [Servo] He's gonna
ultra-bright him to death!

2090
01:19:18,355 --> 01:19:22,192
♪ What would you say
if I sang out of tune ♪

2091
01:19:22,792 --> 01:19:25,795
(loud whirring)

2092
01:19:25,828 --> 01:19:29,967
- [Mike] I'll circle in and
get it some of that plaque.

2093
01:19:30,567 --> 01:19:33,337
(twanging sound)

2094
01:19:36,372 --> 01:19:37,573
- [Phantom] Attention, gunners!

2095
01:19:37,607 --> 01:19:39,642
Blast him with every
available battery!

2096
01:19:39,675 --> 01:19:42,345
Automatic track and fire!

2097
01:19:42,412 --> 01:19:43,913
- [Servo] Okay, a little
this, a little that,

2098
01:19:43,947 --> 01:19:45,782
strike up to this over here...

2099
01:19:45,815 --> 01:19:47,683
(loud explosions)
Oh!

2100
01:19:47,717 --> 01:19:48,518
- [Crow] Is this worth it--

2101
01:19:48,552 --> 01:19:50,453
Ha-ha, no I'll save it.

2102
01:19:51,822 --> 01:19:55,158
(Phantom laughs evilly)

2103
01:19:56,358 --> 01:19:58,762
- [Phantom] So much for
that Prince of Space!

2104
01:19:58,795 --> 01:20:01,463
Nothing, not even he can
resist the devastating effect

2105
01:20:01,498 --> 01:20:04,100
of my thorian bombs.
- What?

2106
01:20:04,133 --> 01:20:06,335
- [Phantom] Now, let's get
on with our ceremony, eh?

2107
01:20:06,368 --> 01:20:08,338
(laughs evilly)
- Oh, don't.

2108
01:20:08,372 --> 01:20:11,708
Doesn't he realize
how forced it sounds?

2109
01:20:13,075 --> 01:20:15,078
Ugh, those eggs.

2110
01:20:15,112 --> 01:20:16,078
- Alright, Macken.

2111
01:20:16,112 --> 01:20:18,215
You first, get a move on!

2112
01:20:19,415 --> 01:20:20,750
- No!

2113
01:20:20,783 --> 01:20:21,952
Don't take Macken!

2114
01:20:21,985 --> 01:20:23,353
- [Crow] Now we isolate
our first contestant

2115
01:20:23,387 --> 01:20:24,787
in a soundproof booth!

2116
01:20:24,820 --> 01:20:27,023
- Leave him alone!
- Hey! What are you doing?

2117
01:20:27,057 --> 01:20:29,558
(doctors shout at the same time)

2118
01:20:29,592 --> 01:20:32,262
- [Mike] Another beer here.

2119
01:20:32,295 --> 01:20:34,998
(loud zinging)

2120
01:20:35,032 --> 01:20:38,968
- [Servo] Back to
my dry goods stores.

2121
01:20:39,002 --> 01:20:41,705
- [Crow] (chuckles)
Seeing these guys,

2122
01:20:41,738 --> 01:20:44,607
it's hard to believe human
beings ever have sex.

2123
01:20:44,640 --> 01:20:47,210
(loud zinging)

2124
01:20:47,243 --> 01:20:48,978
(henchman gasps)
- No!

2125
01:20:48,978 --> 01:20:51,213
- He wasn't killed!
- What?

2126
01:20:51,247 --> 01:20:54,750
(thrilling music)
- Hello!

2127
01:20:56,218 --> 01:20:57,420
- Prince of Space!

2128
01:20:57,453 --> 01:20:59,122
You're still alive, are you?

2129
01:20:59,155 --> 01:21:00,523
- Of course I am.

2130
01:21:00,557 --> 01:21:02,458
And I will keep fighting

2131
01:21:02,492 --> 01:21:05,528
to protect the people
who call upon me

2132
01:21:05,562 --> 01:21:07,930
to save them from
your domination!

2133
01:21:07,963 --> 01:21:09,065
- Blast him!

2134
01:21:09,098 --> 01:21:11,000
(loud zinging)

2135
01:21:11,033 --> 01:21:12,268
- [Servo] Ah, I
didn't say blast,

2136
01:21:12,302 --> 01:21:14,570
I said rest him, rest him,
- Listen!

2137
01:21:14,603 --> 01:21:17,007
I call upon you to surrender!

2138
01:21:17,040 --> 01:21:18,742
To release these Earthlings!

2139
01:21:18,775 --> 01:21:21,612
To return them to wherever
you took them from

2140
01:21:21,645 --> 01:21:24,547
and to cease your evil
plotting once and for all!

2141
01:21:24,580 --> 01:21:26,048
- [Mike] You can't see me!

2142
01:21:26,082 --> 01:21:28,852
(thrilling music)

2143
01:21:28,885 --> 01:21:31,387
(loud racket)

2144
01:21:32,988 --> 01:21:35,258
- Come on, Professor!
- Prince of Space!

2145
01:21:35,292 --> 01:21:36,192
- [Servo] It's Michael Jeter,

2146
01:21:36,225 --> 01:21:37,293
of course it's Prince of Space!

2147
01:21:37,327 --> 01:21:39,862
(loud explosion)

2148
01:21:39,895 --> 01:21:42,465
(loud zinging)

2149
01:21:45,302 --> 01:21:48,605
- [Mike] Oh, our
collective headaches!

2150
01:21:48,638 --> 01:21:52,275
- [Crow] Mouse trap!
(robots hum)

2151
01:21:52,308 --> 01:21:55,412
("MST3K Love Theme")

2152
01:21:58,748 --> 01:22:00,450
- You, turn off
the reserve power!

2153
01:22:00,483 --> 01:22:02,718
Switch on the heating
current to that griddle!

2154
01:22:02,752 --> 01:22:05,888
Now that I've got him I'm
gonna broil him alive!

2155
01:22:05,922 --> 01:22:08,592
(laughs evilly)

2156
01:22:10,027 --> 01:22:12,895
- [Crow] I hope he has his
tanning goggles on! (laughs)

2157
01:22:12,928 --> 01:22:14,730
(loud whirring)
- Here come the deadly

2158
01:22:14,763 --> 01:22:15,932
fly rod cases.

2159
01:22:17,867 --> 01:22:19,102
- [Servo] Dearly beloved,
we are gathered here

2160
01:22:19,135 --> 01:22:20,870
to get through this
thing called life!

2161
01:22:20,903 --> 01:22:23,573
(loud whirring)

2162
01:22:24,773 --> 01:22:27,510
- [Mike] Careful,
sweetie, no rain.

2163
01:22:28,845 --> 01:22:32,382
- [Crow] Gentlemen,
prepare to be super soaked!

2164
01:22:32,415 --> 01:22:35,918
- [Mike] No one can
resist my, uh, things!

2165
01:22:37,320 --> 01:22:39,022
- [Servo] Rapid deployment
system leaves no time

2166
01:22:39,055 --> 01:22:39,888
to react!

2167
01:22:42,058 --> 01:22:44,860
- [Crow] Yeah, the
things are comin' out.

2168
01:22:44,893 --> 01:22:46,628
Come on out, varmint!

2169
01:22:48,398 --> 01:22:52,568
- [Mike] Shouldn't have
let Mom make my costume!

2170
01:22:53,503 --> 01:22:55,072
I am saving up such a laugh.

2171
01:22:55,938 --> 01:22:57,340
- He's well cooked.

2172
01:22:57,373 --> 01:22:58,708
Enough!
- Right!

2173
01:23:01,277 --> 01:23:02,178
- [Servo] Steamed
Prince of Space

2174
01:23:02,212 --> 01:23:03,680
or fried and beer-battered?

2175
01:23:03,713 --> 01:23:07,850
- (gasps) Prince is alive!
- D'oh! I was hidin' here!

2176
01:23:08,552 --> 01:23:09,452
- Enough of this!

2177
01:23:09,485 --> 01:23:10,653
When will you ever learn?

2178
01:23:10,687 --> 01:23:12,188
Your guns won't work on me?

2179
01:23:12,222 --> 01:23:13,457
- Kill him!
(Crow groans)

2180
01:23:13,490 --> 01:23:17,360
- [Mike] (chuckles)
New plan, sir!

2181
01:23:17,393 --> 01:23:18,662
- Fire lasers!

2182
01:23:18,695 --> 01:23:19,862
(loud zinging)

2183
01:23:19,895 --> 01:23:21,430
- [Crow] C'mon, movie's over.

2184
01:23:21,463 --> 01:23:22,498
Let's just go.

2185
01:23:22,532 --> 01:23:25,102
(loud zinging)

2186
01:23:27,270 --> 01:23:29,838
- Put Debbie on hold for a sec.

2187
01:23:32,242 --> 01:23:34,510
- [Mike] Sick,
angry, a turtle...

2188
01:23:34,543 --> 01:23:37,113
(thrilling music)
(loud zinging)

2189
01:23:37,113 --> 01:23:38,280
- [Crow] Oh, I suppose
that's it for me!

2190
01:23:38,313 --> 01:23:39,515
Yup, I'm dead.

2191
01:23:40,783 --> 01:23:41,583
- Give up?

2192
01:23:41,617 --> 01:23:42,852
Or I have to kill you!

2193
01:23:42,885 --> 01:23:45,555
(loud zinging)
- Well, I can't back that up!

2194
01:23:45,588 --> 01:23:48,858
(loud explosions)
- No!

2195
01:23:50,560 --> 01:23:52,328
- [Mike] You'll never
defeat me, bye now!

2196
01:23:52,362 --> 01:23:53,863
- [Crow] Into the giblet mobile!

2197
01:23:53,897 --> 01:23:56,332
(thrilling music)

2198
01:23:56,365 --> 01:23:57,367
- Now's our chance!

2199
01:23:57,400 --> 01:23:58,668
Come on, follow me!
- Yes!

2200
01:23:58,702 --> 01:24:01,838
- [Servo] I have no
objective whatsoever!

2201
01:24:01,872 --> 01:24:02,705
- [Doctor] Where are you going?

2202
01:24:02,738 --> 01:24:03,773
- Follow me! Quickly!

2203
01:24:03,807 --> 01:24:06,042
C'mon, c'mon!
- Follow him!

2204
01:24:06,075 --> 01:24:07,310
(thrilling music)

2205
01:24:07,343 --> 01:24:08,545
- [Servo] We'll just run
potty and then we'll go!

2206
01:24:08,578 --> 01:24:10,313
- [Crow] Mike, I swear
I am never gonna forget

2207
01:24:10,380 --> 01:24:13,450
what the Japanese did
to us with this movie.

2208
01:24:13,483 --> 01:24:14,650
- Come on, this way!

2209
01:24:14,683 --> 01:24:16,318
- [Prince] No, wait, look out!

2210
01:24:16,352 --> 01:24:18,988
(Mike and robots gasp)
- We're trapped!

2211
01:24:19,022 --> 01:24:20,390
- Not yet, come, this way!

2212
01:24:20,423 --> 01:24:22,425
- No, wait, stop!
- What?

2213
01:24:23,627 --> 01:24:24,660
- [Servo] Wait, stop, this way!

2214
01:24:24,693 --> 01:24:25,795
Now, run! No, wait!

2215
01:24:25,828 --> 01:24:26,863
Come on, no look out!

2216
01:24:26,897 --> 01:24:27,830
Wait, stop!

2217
01:24:29,232 --> 01:24:30,867
- [Mike] Prince of Space!

2218
01:24:30,900 --> 01:24:31,802
- Hurry!

2219
01:24:31,835 --> 01:24:32,635
Come this way!

2220
01:24:32,668 --> 01:24:33,637
- No, wait!

2221
01:24:33,670 --> 01:24:34,803
Is that the way out?

2222
01:24:34,837 --> 01:24:36,372
- Of course, come on!

2223
01:24:36,405 --> 01:24:37,640
- [Crow] Wait!
Probably it isn't!

2224
01:24:37,673 --> 01:24:38,475
No, I'll follow you!

2225
01:24:38,508 --> 01:24:40,443
Wait, Prince of Space!

2226
01:24:40,477 --> 01:24:42,278
- [Servo] The Ritz
Brothers have more dignity!

2227
01:24:42,345 --> 01:24:45,148
(doctors shout at the same time)

2228
01:24:45,182 --> 01:24:46,182
- Calm down!

2229
01:24:47,517 --> 01:24:49,685
- [Servo] Okay, now panic.

2230
01:24:51,053 --> 01:24:53,490
- Caught like rats in a trap!

2231
01:24:53,523 --> 01:24:56,025
You'll be safe enough here.

2232
01:24:56,058 --> 01:24:57,727
I'm leaving for Earth now.

2233
01:24:57,760 --> 01:24:58,928
But when I come back, I'll have

2234
01:24:58,962 --> 01:25:01,363
a very special kind
of death for you,

2235
01:25:01,397 --> 01:25:03,933
my dear Prince of Space!

2236
01:25:03,967 --> 01:25:05,135
Goodbye.

2237
01:25:05,168 --> 01:25:06,268
- [Crow] So he
has a quick errand

2238
01:25:06,302 --> 01:25:08,972
before he kills Prince of Space.

2239
01:25:11,073 --> 01:25:13,843
- [Servo] What, what
are you lookin' at?

2240
01:25:13,877 --> 01:25:15,812
- I had a very good reason
for not killing him now.

2241
01:25:15,845 --> 01:25:18,648
He's going to prepare for
blast off in his flagship.

2242
01:25:18,682 --> 01:25:20,650
And unfortunately it's
the only ship available

2243
01:25:20,683 --> 01:25:22,218
that will take
you back to Earth.

2244
01:25:22,252 --> 01:25:24,253
Now, all of you
stay close behind me

2245
01:25:24,287 --> 01:25:27,357
and do exactly what
I tell you to do.

2246
01:25:29,958 --> 01:25:31,693
(loud zinging)
- Okay, now watch more.

2247
01:25:31,727 --> 01:25:32,795
There you go.

2248
01:25:36,198 --> 01:25:39,635
- [Servo] Some more,
yes, good watching...

2249
01:25:39,668 --> 01:25:42,905
- [Crow] My grill
lighter is saving us!

2250
01:25:44,107 --> 01:25:47,543
- [Servo] Oh, we are
more interested now!

2251
01:25:47,577 --> 01:25:51,713
- [Mike] Why is he melting
semi-sweet chocolate?

2252
01:25:53,115 --> 01:25:55,017
- [Crow] (chuckles) Hey,
guys, watch this, watch this.

2253
01:25:55,050 --> 01:25:56,018
My arthritis!

2254
01:25:56,052 --> 01:25:57,353
Oh, my spastic colon!

2255
01:25:57,387 --> 01:25:58,888
- Oh, my gout!
- Oh, my bad knee!

2256
01:25:58,922 --> 01:26:00,390
- Oh, my baldness!

2257
01:26:00,423 --> 01:26:04,027
(thrilling music)

2258
01:26:04,060 --> 01:26:06,963
- [Crow] Prince of
Crossing Guards!

2259
01:26:11,500 --> 01:26:15,605
- [Servo] Would you get
back further, you morons!

2260
01:26:17,207 --> 01:26:19,575
- [Prince] Stop
right where you are!

2261
01:26:19,608 --> 01:26:21,343
(henchmen shout
at the same time)

2262
01:26:21,377 --> 01:26:22,612
- Oh, I love him!
- Let's get his autograph!

2263
01:26:22,612 --> 01:26:24,947
- You fools, he's all alone!

2264
01:26:28,383 --> 01:26:29,818
- Stand where you are!

2265
01:26:29,852 --> 01:26:31,220
The first man who walks down
the ramp will be signing

2266
01:26:31,253 --> 01:26:32,455
his own death warrant!

2267
01:26:32,488 --> 01:26:33,990
I've booby trapped
the whole thing

2268
01:26:34,023 --> 01:26:35,725
and your own thorian
bombs will blast you

2269
01:26:35,758 --> 01:26:37,693
into the next world!

2270
01:26:37,727 --> 01:26:39,262
- You lie.
- You can find out

2271
01:26:39,295 --> 01:26:41,330
pretty easily whether I'm
telling you the truth.

2272
01:26:41,363 --> 01:26:44,700
Look behind you
in that corridor.

2273
01:26:44,733 --> 01:26:46,335
- [Crow] Oh, gross,
stain in the rug!

2274
01:26:46,368 --> 01:26:49,272
- Alright, then I surrender!

2275
01:26:49,305 --> 01:26:50,507
- [Servo] They
locked themselves.

2276
01:26:50,540 --> 01:26:51,807
- [Prince] Get back,
get out of sight!

2277
01:26:51,840 --> 01:26:53,943
- Capture them for hostages!

2278
01:26:53,977 --> 01:26:57,713
- [Crow] So no accumulated
memory whatsoever!

2279
01:26:58,648 --> 01:26:59,848
- Come on.

2280
01:26:59,882 --> 01:27:02,218
Why don't you try
to board your ship?

2281
01:27:02,252 --> 01:27:05,355
- Why you!
- Your brother's bad, too!

2282
01:27:06,222 --> 01:27:08,625
- Oh, Prince! (mumbles)

2283
01:27:08,658 --> 01:27:11,060
Are you alright?
- Quiet down.

2284
01:27:11,093 --> 01:27:12,395
We haven't a moment to lose!

2285
01:27:12,428 --> 01:27:13,863
Everybody board the
ship right away!

2286
01:27:13,897 --> 01:27:15,097
- What about you?

2287
01:27:15,130 --> 01:27:16,432
- I will stay here till
you're safe on your way.

2288
01:27:16,465 --> 01:27:17,767
(loud racket)
- What's that?

2289
01:27:17,800 --> 01:27:19,035
- Go on, hurry!

2290
01:27:19,068 --> 01:27:20,437
- Run!
- Yes, yes!

2291
01:27:20,470 --> 01:27:21,737
- [Crow] Next, the
Prince will sew name tags

2292
01:27:21,770 --> 01:27:23,172
in their underwear.

2293
01:27:23,205 --> 01:27:24,807
Bunch of babies.

2294
01:27:24,840 --> 01:27:27,877
Yeah, I need those guys like I
need another one-inch wiener!

2295
01:27:27,910 --> 01:27:31,213
(thrilling music)
- Keep pushing, men!

2296
01:27:31,247 --> 01:27:33,082
We're almost out
of our atmosphere!

2297
01:27:33,115 --> 01:27:36,118
(loud explosion)

2298
01:27:36,152 --> 01:27:39,655
(Mike grunts and groans)

2299
01:27:39,688 --> 01:27:42,092
(loud screams)
(loud explosion)

2300
01:27:42,125 --> 01:27:43,225
- [Crow] My coup!

2301
01:27:43,258 --> 01:27:45,160
My beautiful,
beautiful coup! (sobs)

2302
01:27:45,193 --> 01:27:48,263
(robots cluck sadly)

2303
01:27:52,035 --> 01:27:53,302
- [Mike] If we'd
built this up to code,

2304
01:27:53,335 --> 01:27:56,138
this never would have happened!

2305
01:27:56,172 --> 01:27:57,507
(loud explosion)
- Ah yes.

2306
01:27:57,540 --> 01:27:59,508
The ancient Japanese
tradition of blowing up models

2307
01:27:59,542 --> 01:28:01,410
at the end of the movie!

2308
01:28:01,443 --> 01:28:03,245
- [Mike] The blast of these
bedrock claim the lives

2309
01:28:03,312 --> 01:28:06,582
of Frederick R. Flintstone
and Barnabas Rubble today.

2310
01:28:06,615 --> 01:28:09,652
(loud zinging)

2311
01:28:09,685 --> 01:28:11,820
- [Crow] And a proud,
noble civilization

2312
01:28:11,853 --> 01:28:13,757
dies out sometimes.

2313
01:28:13,790 --> 01:28:17,960
This loser civilization,
however, will not be missed!

2314
01:28:19,528 --> 01:28:21,330
- Dr. Macken, Dr. Macken!

2315
01:28:21,363 --> 01:28:22,732
- [Servo] I'm wet again!

2316
01:28:22,765 --> 01:28:24,600
- The other mag pilot's
working perfectly!

2317
01:28:24,633 --> 01:28:25,968
We're on a direct
course for Earth!

2318
01:28:26,002 --> 01:28:27,370
- Wonderful!
- And look there

2319
01:28:27,403 --> 01:28:28,303
on the visual screen!

2320
01:28:28,337 --> 01:28:29,805
The one we owe everything to!

2321
01:28:29,838 --> 01:28:34,010
- (gasps) It's the
Prince of Space!

2322
01:28:35,177 --> 01:28:36,378
He wouldn't even
let us say thanks.

2323
01:28:36,378 --> 01:28:37,280
Who knows if we'll
ever see him again?

2324
01:28:37,313 --> 01:28:38,715
- Say, we'd better radio ahead.

2325
01:28:38,748 --> 01:28:39,682
Tell the others we're safe
and we're coming home!

2326
01:28:39,715 --> 01:28:40,983
Thanks to Prince of Space!

2327
01:28:41,017 --> 01:28:42,585
(doctors agree at the same time)

2328
01:28:42,618 --> 01:28:44,220
- [Servo] On their own,
the giant infant scientists

2329
01:28:44,253 --> 01:28:48,257
survived another minute
and then crashed.

2330
01:28:48,290 --> 01:28:49,658
- [Mike] Meanwhile
all the boot centers

2331
01:28:49,692 --> 01:28:52,628
get duller and less black.

2332
01:28:52,662 --> 01:28:55,432
- [Crow] And yet,
I feel so empty.

2333
01:28:56,632 --> 01:28:57,533
- [Servo] You know,
this movie made me

2334
01:28:57,567 --> 01:28:59,568
wanna renounce my Toyota.

2335
01:29:03,005 --> 01:29:04,540
Oh, it's the end!

2336
01:29:04,573 --> 01:29:06,742
This movie cannon's
enough for me!

2337
01:29:06,775 --> 01:29:09,612
- [Mike] But it's
Prince of Space!

2338
01:29:10,647 --> 01:29:13,148
(doors close)

2339
01:29:21,890 --> 01:29:23,325
- Okay, okay, okay.

2340
01:29:23,358 --> 01:29:25,127
I'm a satellite of
love, right, right?

2341
01:29:25,160 --> 01:29:28,463
There's no time lags, Mike's
not a puny little robot.

2342
01:29:28,497 --> 01:29:29,298
- Nope, I--

2343
01:29:29,332 --> 01:29:30,733
Well, I don't think so.

2344
01:29:30,767 --> 01:29:31,967
- 'Cause I tell you guys,
you get to the point

2345
01:29:32,000 --> 01:29:34,503
where you just wanna go,
"Wormhole, back off!"

2346
01:29:34,537 --> 01:29:35,872
- No, I hear you.

2347
01:29:35,905 --> 01:29:37,307
But it seems like
everything's back to normal.

2348
01:29:37,340 --> 01:29:39,708
Oh, you guys know
my wife, Krankor.

2349
01:29:39,742 --> 01:29:41,843
(robots scream)
- Get me outta here!

2350
01:29:41,877 --> 01:29:46,015
(Phantom laughs evilly)
- (laughs) That was good!

2351
01:29:46,748 --> 01:29:47,817
We got 'em, Krankor,

2352
01:29:47,850 --> 01:29:49,052
thanks a lot!
- We certainly got them

2353
01:29:49,085 --> 01:29:50,920
that time! (laughs evilly)
- Yeah.

2354
01:29:50,953 --> 01:29:52,322
Yeah, well, there's no reason
for you to hang around.

2355
01:29:52,355 --> 01:29:54,390
You can take off.
- They ran like fools!

2356
01:29:54,423 --> 01:29:56,892
(laughs evilly)
- Yeah, I guess

2357
01:29:56,925 --> 01:29:58,427
they did, Krankor.

2358
01:29:58,460 --> 01:30:00,128
- We pulled the wool
over their eyes!

2359
01:30:00,162 --> 01:30:01,263
(laughs evilly)
- You know what,

2360
01:30:01,297 --> 01:30:02,898
Krankor wants to leave, alright?

2361
01:30:02,932 --> 01:30:04,133
- Oh, do you?

2362
01:30:04,167 --> 01:30:05,535
Well, you may be
interested to know

2363
01:30:05,568 --> 01:30:06,968
that I've already conquered
your puny satellite

2364
01:30:07,002 --> 01:30:08,570
and then you have no defense--
(Mike shouts)

2365
01:30:08,603 --> 01:30:11,473
Oh, oh! Oh, please
don't hurt me!

2366
01:30:11,507 --> 01:30:12,675
- Krankor.

2367
01:30:12,708 --> 01:30:14,577
- Mike, Crow, Servo, Krankor!

2368
01:30:14,610 --> 01:30:16,645
We're orbiting the planet
that looks like ours!

2369
01:30:16,645 --> 01:30:18,815
- Earth, wow!
- Not sure.

2370
01:30:18,848 --> 01:30:19,782
- Oh, really?
- Yes!

2371
01:30:19,815 --> 01:30:21,350
- It is?
- I think.

2372
01:30:21,383 --> 01:30:22,618
- Would you knock
it off, Mrs. F.

2373
01:30:22,652 --> 01:30:23,887
How about you?

2374
01:30:23,920 --> 01:30:27,123
Do you know where we
are or when we are?

2375
01:30:27,157 --> 01:30:28,825
- I don't know, Mike.

2376
01:30:28,858 --> 01:30:32,027
There's no sign of Bobo but
there are marble columns

2377
01:30:32,060 --> 01:30:34,097
and intricate frescoes.

2378
01:30:34,130 --> 01:30:36,198
- Evidently a sewage
system of some sort.

2379
01:30:36,232 --> 01:30:39,102
- Could it possibly be--
(trumpets blare)

2380
01:30:39,135 --> 01:30:42,070
- Welcome to Roman Times!
- Guards! (claps)

2381
01:30:42,103 --> 01:30:45,942
Seize them!
(thrilling music)

